2026-05-19T02:56:02.084021Z  INFO ThreadId(13) universal_search_service::service: 669: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, here are the comprehensive technical specifications for the Phi-3.5-Vision-Instruct model:\n\n## **Model Specifications**\n\n**Architecture & Size:**\n- **Parameters:** 4.2 billion (4.2B)\n- **Architecture:** Transformer-based with image encoder, connector, projector, and Phi-3 Mini language model core\n- **Context Window:** 128K tokens\n- **Max Output:** 4K tokens\n- **Release Date:** August 2024\n- **License:** MIT\n\n**Training Details:**\n- **Training Data:** 500B tokens (vision + text)\n- **Training Hardware:** 256 A100-80G GPUs\n- **Training Time:** 6 days (July-August 2024)\n- **Data Cutoff:** March 15, 2024\n\n## **VRAM Requirements**\n\nThe model supports multiple quantization levels for flexible deployment:\n\n| Quantization | VRAM Required | Model Size |\n|--------------|---------------|------------|\n| **Q4_K_M**   | 2 GB          | 2 GB       |\n| **Q5_K_M**   | 3 GB          | 3 GB       |\n| **Q8**       | 3 GB          | 3 GB       |\n| **FP16**     | 6 GB          | 6 GB       |\n\n**Minimum System Requirements:**\n- **VRAM:** 2GB (Q4) to 6GB (FP16)\n- **RAM:** 16GB minimum, 32GB recommended\n- **CPU:** Modern CPU (Ryzen 5/Intel i5 or better)\n\n## **Vision Capabilities**\n\n**Core Multimodal Functions:**\n- Single and multi-frame image understanding\n- Visual question answering\n- Optical character recognition (OCR)\n- Chart and table understanding\n- Document intelligence\n- Multi-image comparison and analysis\n- Video summarization\n- Sequential image reasoning\n\n**Supported Input Formats:**\n- Images (single and multiple)\n- Text prompts\n- Chat-style conversation format\n\n**Performance Benchmarks:**\n- **MMMU:** 43.0\n- **MMBench:** 81.9\n- **TextVQA:** 72.0\n- **BLINK (multi-frame):** 57.0 overall\n- **Video-MME:** 50.8 overall\n\n## **Technical Implementation**\n\n**Software Requirements:**\n- PyTorch\n- Transformers\n- Flash-Attention (optional but recommended for performance)\n- Python packages: numpy, Pillow, requests, torch, torchvision, accelerate\n\n**Tested GPU Compatibility:**\n- NVIDIA A100, A6000, H100\n- Consumer GPUs: RTX 4090, RTX 4080, RTX 3090, etc.\n- AMD GPUs: RX 7900 XTX, MI300X, etc.\n- Apple Silicon: M2/M3/M4 series\n\n## **Key Features**\n\n- **Efficient Design:** Optimized for memory/compute constrained environments\n- **Instruction Following:** Enhanced through supervised fine-tuning and direct preference optimization\n- **Safety Alignment:** Uses RLHF and safety post-training techniques\n- **English Focus:** Primarily optimized for English language tasks\n- **Commercial Use:** Suitable for broad commercial and research applications\n\nThe model represents Microsoft's effort to create a compact yet powerful multimodal AI that can handle complex visual reasoning tasks while maintaining efficiency for deployment in resource-constrained environments.\n\n**Sources:**\n- Hugging Face Model Card: https://huggingface.co/microsoft/Phi-3.5-vision-instruct\n- LocalAI Computer VRAM Requirements: https://localai.computer/models/microsoft-phi-3.5-vision-instruct\n- Open Laboratory Technical Report: https://openlaboratory.com/models/phi3_5_vision/","type":"text"}],"id":"054efe16532e43e6ae9ab46397645b73","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":22731,"output_tokens":853}}
