2026-05-24T16:07:01.379639Z  INFO ThreadId(15) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, I can provide you with a comprehensive answer about copying LVM thin volumes between pools in Proxmox.\n\n## Direct Answer: No Native `lvconvert` Method for Cross-Pool Migration\n\n**LVM does not provide a direct `lvconvert` command to move a thin volume from one thin pool to another.** The `lvconvert` command is designed for converting between different LV types (e.g., linear to thin, thick to thin-pool), not for moving thin volumes between existing pools.\n\n## Recommended Manual Migration Methods\n\n### Method 1: Using `dd` (Block-level Copy)\n\nThis is the most straightforward approach for copying the entire volume:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Create a new thin volume in the destination pool with the same virtual size\nlvcreate -V <virtual_size> -T <destination_vg>/<destination_pool> -n <new_volume_name>\n\n# 2. Copy data using dd (ensure source is not in use or take a snapshot first)\ndd if=/dev/<source_vg>/<source_thin_volume> of=/dev/<destination_vg>/<new_volume_name> bs=4M status=progress\n```\n\n**Important:** The source volume should be offline or you should create a snapshot first to ensure data consistency.\n\n### Method 2: Using Filesystem Tools (if volume contains a filesystem)\n\nIf the thin volume contains a filesystem, you can:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Create and mount the new thin volume\nlvcreate -V <virtual_size> -T <destination_vg>/<destination_pool> -n <new_volume_name>\nmkfs.<filesystem_type> /dev/<destination_vg>/<new_volume_name>\nmount /dev/<destination_vg>/<new_volume_name> /mnt/destination\n\n# 2. Mount the source volume (or a snapshot) read-only\nmount -o ro /dev/<source_vg>/<source_thin_volume> /mnt/source\n\n# 3. Copy files using rsync or cp\nrsync -aHAX /mnt/source/ /mnt/destination/\n# or\ncp -a /mnt/source/* /mnt/destination/\n\n# 4. Unmount both\numount /mnt/source /mnt/destination\n```\n\n### Method 3: Using LVM Snapshots and `thin_delta` (Advanced)\n\nFor incremental synchronization, you can use the thin provisioning tools:\n\n```bash\n# This method is more complex and requires the thin-provisioning-tools package\n# It involves creating snapshots and using thin_delta to transfer only changed blocks\n```\n\n## Proxmox-Specific Considerations\n\nIn Proxmox, thin volumes are typically stored as:\n- VM disk images: `vm-<VMID>-disk-<N>`\n- Container volumes: `vm-<CTID>-vol-<name>`\n\nThese are located in `/dev/pve/data` (or your configured thin pool).\n\n**To migrate a VM disk between pools:**\n\n1. **Stop the VM** to ensure data consistency\n2. **Create a new volume** in the destination pool using `qm set` or manually with LVM\n3. **Copy the data** using one of the methods above\n4. **Update VM configuration** to point to the new volume\n5. **Remove the old volume** after verification\n\n## Important Limitations\n\n- **No atomic operation:** Migration is not instantaneous and requires downtime\n- **Space requirements:** The destination pool must have enough free space for the new volume\n- **Performance:** Copying large volumes can be time-consuming\n- **Thin-specific features:** Snapshots and clones cannot be directly migrated; you must copy the base volume and recreate snapshots if needed\n\n## Alternative: Storage Migration via Proxmox GUI\n\nProxmox provides a built-in storage migration feature that can move VMs between storage backends, including between different LVM thin pools. This is often the safest approach as it handles all the details:\n\n1. Go to **Datacenter > Storage**\n2. Add both thin pools as storage\n3. Use **qm move disk** or **pct move volume** commands, or use the GUI to migrate the VM/CT\n\n## Sources\n\n- Proxmox VE Wiki - Storage: LVM Thin: https://pve.proxmox.com/wiki/Storage:_LVM_Thin\n- LVM thin man page (lvmthin(7)): https://www.man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/lvmthin.7.html\n- lvconvert man page: https://www.man7.org/linux/man-pages/man8/lvconvert.8.html","type":"text"}],"id":"1c94fa9baac241bf88961bc3251d6cfb","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":88276,"input_tokens":26172,"output_tokens":967}}
