2026-05-25T13:18:06.438331Z  INFO ThreadId(17) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, here is the comprehensive information about FlashInfer's SM_120a Blackwell support as of May 2026:\n\n## Current FlashInfer SM_120a Support Status\n\n**Architecture Support:**\n- FlashInfer officially supports **Blackwell Lite (SM 12.x)** architecture, which includes both SM_120a (RTX 50 series) and SM_121a (DGX Spark/GB10)\n- The library detects compute capability at runtime and selects appropriate kernels for SM 12.x devices\n- Support was added starting in **FlashInfer v0.5.2** and has been progressively improved\n\n**Latest Release Information:**\n- The most recent stable release is **FlashInfer v0.6.11.post3** (released May 15, 2026)\n- Pre-compiled cubins are available through the `flashinfer-cubin` package (latest: 0.6.11.post3)\n- Wheels are built targeting SM12x architecture for CUDA ≥ 12.9\n\n**Backend Support for SM_120a:**\n- **Attention**: FA2 (fallback), XQA MLA, CuTe DSL\n- **GEMM**: CUTLASS, cuDNN, B12X (NVFP4 GEMM for SM120/121)\n- **Quantization**: FP4/FP8 support with NVFP4/MXFP4 capabilities\n- **MoE**: CUTLASS and B12X fused MoE kernels\n\n**Known Issues and Limitations:**\n1. **B12X Backend**: The high-performance NVFP4 GEMM backend is currently excluded from automatic dispatch on SM121 due to heuristic checks requiring `minor == 0` (SM120 only)\n2. **GDN (Gated Delta Net)**: Prefill/decode kernels are broken on SM121 - they're compiled with SM90a flags and incompatible\n3. **Wheel Build Gap**: Prebuilt wheels only include `120f` (family) target, not `120a` or `121a`, which means NVFP4/MXFP4 MMA instructions require JIT compilation\n4. **Test Coverage**: Several tests explicitly skip SM121 or have xfail markers\n\n**Recent Improvements (May 2026):**\n- Multiple PRs addressing SM121 compatibility issues have been merged\n- Fixed TMEM allocation column map to include SM121\n- Enabled BMM MXFP8 tests for SM12x\n- Updated documentation to use \"SM12x\" instead of just \"SM120\"\n\n**Community Context:**\nThere is active discussion in the NVIDIA developer forums about SM121 software support gaps, with some users reporting compilation failures and requesting official roadmaps. NVIDIA representatives have confirmed that SM12x support is included from v0.5.3 onward and that wheels are explicitly built targeting SM12x.\n\n## Sources:\n- [FlashInfer GitHub Issue #3170 - DGX Spark (SM121) Current Support Audit](https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/issues/3170)\n- [FlashInfer DeepWiki - Hardware and Backend Support](https://deepwiki.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/1.2-hardware-and-backend-support)\n- [PyPI - flashinfer-cubin 0.6.11.post3](https://pypi.org/project/flashinfer-cubin/)\n- [NVIDIA Developer Forums - DGX Spark Software Support Discussion](https://forums.developer.nvidia.com/t/dgx-spark-sm121-software-support-is-severely-lacking-official-roadmap-needed/357663)","type":"text"}],"id":"67bc2fd14cfc47bdb70479e5a18aba21","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":23052,"input_tokens":51082,"output_tokens":828}}
