2026-05-25T18:34:12.168524Z  INFO ThreadId(14) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, here's a comprehensive tutorial on **LongCat-Video key frame conditioning and seamless transitions**:\n\n## LongCat-Video Key Frame Conditioning Tutorial\n\nLongCat-Video supports multiple generation modes, including **Video Continuation (VC)**, which is specifically designed for seamless transitions by conditioning on previous frames.\n\n### Understanding Video Continuation (VC)\n\nVideo Continuation generates new frames by conditioning on the last `num_cond_frames` frames from an input video. Unlike Image-to-Video (I2V) which uses a single image, VC uses multiple frames to capture motion dynamics and temporal context, producing smooth transitions between segments.\n\n**Key Parameters:**\n- `num_cond_frames`: Number of conditioning frames (default: 13)\n- `num_frames`: Total frames to generate (including conditioning)\n- `use_kv_cache`: Enable KV cache for faster inference (default: True)\n- `enhance_hf`: Use enhanced high-frequency schedule for better detail (default: True)\n\n### Seamless Transition Techniques\n\n#### 1. **Temporal Overlap Strategy**\nWhen extending videos iteratively for long-form content, the system uses overlapping frames between segments:\n\n| Parameter | Value | Purpose |\n|-----------|-------|---------|\n| `num_cond_frames` | 13 | Frames from previous segment used as conditioning |\n| Overlap frames | 13 | Number of frames shared between consecutive segments |\n| New frames per iteration | 80 | `num_frames - num_cond_frames = 93 - 13` |\n\nThis overlap ensures smooth visual continuity between segments.\n\n#### 2. **Prompt Engineering for Transitions**\n\nUse temporal sequencing and motion vocabulary in your prompts:\n\n**Temporal Markers:**\n- \"Initially, ... Then, ... Finally, ...\"\n- \"Gradually transforms from X to Y\"\n- \"Seamlessly transitions to...\"\n\n**Motion Vocabulary:**\n- Verbs: floating, accelerating, dissolving, emerging, circling\n- Adverbs: smoothly, gradually, rapidly, rhythmically, gently\n- Transitions: transforming into, fading to, zooming out to reveal\n\n**Example Prompt:**\n> \"A sleek red sports car driving down a winding coastal highway at sunset. The camera follows alongside the vehicle, capturing reflections of the golden sun on its polished surface. The scene transitions from close-up details of the wheels to a wide aerial shot revealing the dramatic coastline below. Cinematic lighting, photorealistic, 4K quality.\"\n\n#### 3. **Negative Prompts for Quality**\n\nAdd specific exclusions to prevent abrupt changes:\n```\n\"abrupt scene changes, camera shake, color distortion, static, blurred details\"\n```\n\n### Implementation Example\n\n```python\nfrom longcat_video.pipeline_longcat_video import LongCatVideoPipeline\n\n# Initialize pipeline\npipeline = LongCatVideoPipeline(checkpoint_dir=\"./weights/LongCat-Video\")\n\n# Video continuation with seamless transition\nresult = pipeline.generate_vc(\n    video=input_video_frames,  # List of PIL Images\n    prompt=\"Your detailed transition prompt here\",\n    num_frames=93,              # Total frames to generate\n    num_cond_frames=13,         # Use last 13 frames as conditioning\n    resolution=\"720p\",\n    use_kv_cache=True,\n    enhance_hf=True,\n    num_inference_steps=30,\n    guidance_scale=5\n)\n```\n\n### Three-Stage Refinement Pipeline\n\nFor optimal quality, LongCat-Video uses a coarse-to-fine approach:\n\n1. **Base Generation**: 480p with 50 inference steps\n2. **Distillation**: 480p in 16 steps using `cfg_step_lora`\n3. **Refinement**: Upscale to 720p using `refinement_lora` and Block Sparse Attention\n\n### Common Issues and Fixes\n\n**Static or Minimal Movement:**\n- Add motion-specific language to prompts\n- Increase frame count\n- Use dynamic verbs and transition descriptions\n\n**Inconsistent Subject Appearance:**\n- Add \"consistent\" to your prompt\n- Strengthen description of defining features\n- Use negative prompt: \"no changing appearance\"\n\n**Unnatural Motion:**\n- Use organic motion terms (\"flowing,\" \"natural,\" \"smooth\")\n- Avoid contradictory motion directions\n- Add \"realistic physics\" to prompt\n\n### Parameter Recommendations\n\n| Parameter | Recommended Setting |\n|-----------|---------------------|\n| Resolution | 480p for testing; 720p at 30fps for final |\n| num_frames | 150-300 for complete scenes; 300+ for extended sequences |\n| num_inference_steps | 30-40 for balanced quality |\n| guidance_scale | 4-6 for balanced results; 7-10 for strict adherence |\n\n### Sources\n\n- [LongCat-Video Prompt Guide - fal.ai](https://fal.ai/learn/biz/longcat-video-prompt-guide)\n- [LongCat-Video GitHub Repository](https://github.com/meituan-longcat/LongCat-Video)\n- [Video Continuation Technical Documentation](https://deepwiki.com/meituan-longcat/LongCat-Video/4.3-video-continuation-(vc))","type":"text"}],"id":"33709d2de32e44faa6d510005340329f","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":35960,"input_tokens":6296,"output_tokens":1121}}
