2026-05-26T02:04:49.390245Z  INFO ThreadId(14) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"## nvidia-cutlass-dsl: CUTLASS Python DSL (CuTe) Package\n\nThe `nvidia-cutlass-dsl` package is the official PyPI distribution of NVIDIA's CUTLASS Python DSL, providing a Python-native interface for writing high-performance CUDA kernels using CuTe abstractions. It allows developers to author GPU kernels in Python with performance comparable to hand-tuned C++.\n\n### Installation\n\n```bash\npip install nvidia-cutlass-dsl\n```\n\n**Current version:** 4.5.2 (released May 25, 2026)  \n**Python requirement:** ≥ 3.10  \n**Supported CUDA:** 12.x and 13.x  \n**Supported OS:** Linux  \n**Supported GPUs:** Volta (SM70) through Blackwell (SM100/SM120)\n\n### Key Features\n\n- **CuTe DSL**: Low-level programming model consistent with CuTe C++ abstractions (layouts, tensors, hardware atoms, thread hierarchy control)\n- **JIT Compilation**: Fast compilation (seconds) via MLIR backend\n- **Hybrid DSL Design**: Combines AST preprocessing with tracing for flexible metaprogramming\n- **Framework Integration**: Native integration with PyTorch, JAX, and other frameworks via TVM FFI\n- **Tensor Core Optimization**: Targets Ampere, Hopper, and Blackwell Tensor Cores\n\n### Usage Example\n\n```python\nimport cutlass.cute as cute\n\n@cute.kernel\ndef my_kernel():\n    tidx, _, _ = cute.arch.thread_idx()\n    if tidx == 0:\n        cute.printf(\"Hello from GPU!\\n\")\n\n@cute.jit\ndef host():\n    my_kernel().launch(grid=(1, 1, 1), block=(32, 1, 1))\n\nhost()\n```\n\n### Documentation & Resources\n\n- **PyPI Project**: https://pypi.org/project/nvidia-cutlass-dsl/\n- **GitHub Repository**: https://github.com/NVIDIA/cutlass\n- **Official Documentation**: https://docs.nvidia.com/cutlass/latest/media/docs/pythonDSL/cute_dsl.html\n- **CuTe DSL Quick Start**: https://docs.nvidia.com/cutlass/latest/media/docs/pythonDSL/quick_start.html\n\n### Important Notes\n\n- The package is in **public beta** and expected to graduate out of beta by summer 2026.\n- It provides two Python interfaces: **CuTe DSL** (custom kernel authoring) and **cutlass_cppgen** (pre-built operation instantiation).\n- The DSL uses a hybrid approach combining AST and tracing to balance authoring flexibility with performance.\n\n### Citation\n\nIf you use this software in your research, please cite the CUTLASS project as described in the repository's CITATION.cff file.\n\n---\n\n**Sources:**  \n- PyPI project page: https://pypi.org/project/nvidia-cutlass-dsl/  \n- CUTLASS GitHub: https://github.com/NVIDIA/cutlass  \n- CUTLASS Documentation: https://docs.nvidia.com/cutlass/latest/media/docs/pythonDSL/cute_dsl.html","type":"text"}],"id":"3469b6dfaddb4210927e322d02e84583","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":39152,"input_tokens":7211,"output_tokens":663}}
