2026-06-01T06:18:49.140517Z  INFO ThreadId(16) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, here is a comprehensive guide for deploying SGLang with Nemotron-3-Nano-Omni in NVFP4 format on a single RTX 6000 Blackwell GPU with CPU offload memory optimization:\n\n## **SGLang Nemotron-3-Nano-Omni NVFP4 Deployment on RTX 6000 Blackwell**\n\n### **Model Overview**\nThe **NVIDIA Nemotron-3-Nano-Omni** is a 30B-parameter hybrid MoE multimodal model with:\n- **30B total parameters, 3B active per forward pass**\n- **1M token context window**\n- **Unified vision, audio, and text understanding**\n- **NVFP4 quantization** for maximum memory efficiency (requires Blackwell architecture)\n\n### **Hardware Requirements**\n- **GPU**: NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell (96GB VRAM, SM120)\n- **CPU**: Sufficient RAM for offloading (64GB+ recommended)\n- **Software**: CUDA 13.0, PyTorch 2.9.1+, SGLang 0.5.6+\n\n### **Deployment Command for Single GPU with CPU Offload**\n\n```bash\npython3 -m sglang.launch_server \\\n  --model-path nvidia/Nemotron-3-Nano-Omni-30B-A3B-NVFP4 \\\n  --trust-remote-code \\\n  --tp 1 \\\n  --attention-backend flashinfer \\\n  --tool-call-parser qwen3_coder \\\n  --reasoning-parser nano_v3 \\\n  --mem-fraction-static 0.7 \\\n  --max-running-requests 8 \\\n  --cpu-offload-gb 32 \\\n  --quantization modelopt_fp4 \\\n  --kv-cache-dtype fp8_e4m3 \\\n  --host 0.0.0.0 \\\n  --port 30000\n```\n\n### **Key Memory Optimization Parameters**\n\n| Parameter | Purpose | Recommended Value |\n|-----------|---------|-------------------|\n| `--mem-fraction-static` | GPU memory fraction for weights + KV cache | 0.7 (70% of 96GB = 67.2GB) |\n| `--cpu-offload-gb` | CPU memory for offloading (GB) | 32 (adjust based on available RAM) |\n| `--kv-cache-dtype fp8_e4m3` | FP8 KV cache for memory efficiency | Essential for long context |\n| `--max-running-requests` | Concurrency limit | 8-16 (balance throughput vs memory) |\n\n### **Performance Expectations**\nBased on benchmarks from similar configurations:\n- **Throughput**: ~4,300-8,700 tokens/sec total\n- **Time to First Token (TTFT)**: ~50-500ms depending on prompt length\n- **Time per Output Token (TPOT)**: ~20-25ms\n- **MMLU Accuracy**: ~70% with NVFP4 (0.9% lower than BF16)\n\n### **Advanced Optimization Tips**\n\n1. **Memory Management**:\n   - Use `--mem-fraction-static 0.7` to leave headroom for activations\n   - Enable FP8 KV cache (`--kv-cache-dtype fp8_e4m3`) to double context capacity\n   - Set `--cpu-offload-gb` based on available system RAM\n\n2. **Performance Tuning**:\n   - Use FlashInfer backend for optimal SM120 performance\n   - Enable multi-threaded model loading: `--model-loader-extra-config '{\"enable_multithread_load\": true, \"num_threads\": 16}'`\n   - Adjust `--chunked-prefill-size` (4096-32768) for latency/throughput trade-off\n\n3. **CPU Offloading Strategy**:\n   - SGLang's CPU offloading moves inactive model layers to system RAM\n   - Set `--cpu-offload-gb` to 32-64GB depending on available RAM\n   - Monitor system performance; excessive offloading may increase latency\n\n### **Alternative: Without CPU Offload**\nIf you have sufficient GPU memory and want maximum speed:\n\n```bash\npython3 -m sglang.launch_server \\\n  --model-path nvidia/Nemotron-3-Nano-Omni-30B-A3B-NVFP4 \\\n  --trust-remote-code \\\n  --tp 1 \\\n  --attention-backend flashinfer \\\n  --tool-call-parser qwen3_coder \\\n  --reasoning-parser nano_v3 \\\n  --mem-fraction-static 0.85 \\\n  --max-running-requests 16 \\\n  --quantization modelopt_fp4 \\\n  --kv-cache-dtype fp8_e4m3 \\\n  --host 0.0.0.0 \\\n  --port 30000\n```\n\n### **Monitoring and Troubleshooting**\n- Use `nvidia-smi` to monitor GPU memory usage\n- Check SGLang logs for memory allocation details\n- If OOM occurs, reduce `--mem-fraction-static` or `--max-running-requests`\n- For latency issues, reduce `--chunked-prefill-size`\n\n### **Sources**\n- [SGLang Nemotron-3-Nano-Omni Documentation](https://docs.sglang.io/cookbook/autoregressive/NVIDIA/Nemotron3-Nano-Omni)\n- [SGLang on RTX 6000 Pro Blackwell Guide](https://github.com/local-inference-lab/rtx6kpro/blob/master/inference-engines/sglang.md)\n- [NVIDIA Developer Forums - SGLang Build Guide](https://forums.developer.nvidia.com/t/build-sglang-from-source-on-blackwell-pro-6000-dgx-spark/360785)\n- [SGLang Performance Tuning Guide](https://deepwiki.com/zhanxxxxxxx/sglang/9.2-performance-tuning-guide)\n\nThis configuration balances memory efficiency with performance, enabling the 30B multimodal model to run on a single RTX 6000 Blackwell GPU while maintaining good throughput and supporting long context windows.","type":"text"}],"id":"315b8ad46fb24d8cab5f4aa52a82f42f","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":59344,"input_tokens":17341,"output_tokens":1395}}
