2026-06-01T08:08:10.831042Z  INFO ThreadId(11) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, I can provide a comprehensive answer about the relationship between sglang, CUDA graph capture, and the libcudart.so.12 vs libcudart.so.13 library compatibility issues.\n\n## Summary\n\n**sglang** is a high-performance serving framework for large language models that extensively uses **CUDA graphs** to optimize inference performance. The recent issue involves **sgl-kernel** (a dependency) being linked against CUDA 12 runtime libraries (`libcudart.so.12`, `libnvrtc.so.12`) while systems like NVIDIA DGX Spark only provide CUDA 13 libraries (`libcudart.so.13`, `libnvrtc.so.13`).\n\n## Key Findings\n\n### 1. SGLang's CUDA Graph System\nSGLang implements advanced CUDA graph optimizations including:\n- **Standard CUDA graphs** for decode operations to eliminate kernel launch overhead\n- **Breakable CUDA graphs** allowing graph breaks at specific points for incompatible operations\n- **Piecewise CUDA graphs** splitting execution into multiple captured segments\n- **torch.compile integration** for additional kernel fusion\n\nThe CUDA graph capture process is managed by `CudaGraphRunner` which handles memory pool initialization, input buffer preparation, warmup passes, and graph capture/replay.\n\n### 2. The libcudart.so.12 vs .13 Compatibility Problem\n**Issue**: sgl-kernel ships binaries (e.g., `sm100/common_ops.abi3.so`) linked against CUDA 12 runtime libraries. On systems with only CUDA 13 installed, this causes import errors:\n```\nImportError: libnvrtc.so.12: cannot open shared object file: No such file or directory\n```\n\n**Root cause**: The wheel was built/linked against CUDA 12, but the target system (DGX Spark with GB10 GPU) only has CUDA 13 toolkit.\n\n### 3. Workarounds\nUsers have reported success with:\n- Installing CUDA 12 runtime libraries alongside CUDA 13 (via conda or pip)\n- Using PyTorch wheels built for CUDA 12.x: `pip install torch --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu124`\n- Container-based solutions that bundle the correct CUDA version\n\n### 4. SGLang's Breakable CUDA Graph Feature\nThis feature is particularly relevant to the library compatibility issue because it allows selective graph breaks, making the system more flexible when certain operations cannot be captured. The implementation uses `BreakableCUDAGraphCapture` and requires `cuda-python` package.\n\n## Sources\n\n1. **SGLang CUDA Graph Implementation**: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/python/sglang/srt/model_executor/cuda_graph_runner.py\n2. **Breakable CUDA Graph Documentation**: https://docs.sglang.io/docs/advanced_features/breakable_cuda_graph\n3. **GitHub Issue - sgl-kernel CUDA 13 incompatibility**: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang-omni/issues/620\n4. **vLLM/DGX Spark libcudart.so.12 issue discussion**: https://huggingface.co/zai-org/GLM-4.7-Flash/discussions/18\n5. **NVIDIA CUDA compatibility documentation**: https://docs.nvidia.com/deploy/cuda-compatibility/why-cuda-compatibility.html\n\nThe core issue is that while CUDA maintains driver-level backward compatibility, applications linked against specific runtime library versions (libcudart.so.X) require those exact versions to be present at runtime unless compatibility shims are provided.","type":"text"}],"id":"faf2f14c996a4dbaa505abc8086b518b","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":44076,"input_tokens":9685,"output_tokens":767}}
2026-06-01T08:42:58.534783Z  INFO ThreadId(17) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"I'll search for information about SGLang's CPU offload memory options for serving.\n\n","type":"text"},{"id":"call_fbc0275884864b1eafa54ac4","input":{"query":"SGLang CPU offload memory options --cpu-offload-gb serving"},"name":"search","type":"tool_use"}],"id":"3f9b72d204ce48e0b44a3b74bde8c899","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":1008,"output_tokens":57}}
2026-06-01T08:43:08.399313Z  INFO ThreadId(17) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on the search results, I found the information about SGLang's CPU offload memory options. Let me provide you with the answer:\n\n## SGLang CPU Offload Memory Options\n\nSGLang provides the `--cpu-offload-gb` flag for CPU offloading during serving. This option allows you to reserve a specific amount of RAM (in gigabytes) for CPU offloading to help manage memory when serving large models.\n\n### Key Parameters:\n\n**`--cpu-offload-gb`**\n- **Description**: How many GBs of RAM to reserve for CPU offloading\n- **Default**: `0` (disabled)\n- **Type**: Integer\n\n### Related Offloading Parameters:\n\nSGLang also provides additional offloading configuration options:\n\n- **`--offload-group-size`**: Number of layers per group in offloading (default: `-1`)\n- **`--offload-num-in-group`**: Number of layers to be offloaded within a group (default: `1`)\n- **`--offload-prefetch-step`**: Steps to prefetch in offloading (default: `1`)\n- **`--offload-mode`**: Mode of offloading (default: `cpu`)\n\n### Usage Example:\n\n```bash\npython -m sglang.launch_server \\\n  --model-path meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3-8B-Instruct \\\n  --cpu-offload-gb 80 \\\n  --mem-fraction-static 0.9\n```\n\n### Additional Memory Management Options:\n\nFor better memory management, you can also adjust:\n\n- **`--mem-fraction-static`**: The fraction of memory used for static allocation (model weights and KV cache memory pool). Default is `0.9`. Use a smaller value if you see out-of-memory errors.\n\n### Source:\n- [SGLang Server Arguments Documentation](https://docs.sglang.io/docs/advanced_features/server_arguments)\n\nThe `--cpu-offload-gb` parameter is particularly useful when you need to serve large models that don't fit entirely in GPU memory, allowing you to offload some computation to CPU RAM.","type":"text"}],"id":"bac9c177c2404bbeb4f92a93abc8f417","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":29773,"output_tokens":454}}
