2026-06-01T11:49:35.577699Z  INFO ThreadId(13) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, I can provide you with information about the SGLang phi4mm multimodal LoRA chunked_sgmv assert error related to vision encoder. Here's what I found:\n\n## Understanding the Issue\n\nThe error appears to be related to the **Chunked SGMV (Segmented Gather Matrix-Vector) LoRA backend** when used with **Phi-4-multimodal** models in SGLang. This is a specialized LoRA implementation that processes LoRA computations in chunks for better hardware utilization.\n\n## Key Technical Components\n\n### 1. **Chunked SGMV Backend**\n- SGLang supports two LoRA backends: `triton` (basic) and `csgmv` (chunked SGMV, default)\n- The `csgmv` backend is optimized for high-concurrency scenarios and achieves 20-80% latency improvements\n- It processes LoRA computations in chunks using `max_lora_chunk_size` parameter (default: 16)\n\n### 2. **Phi-4-Multimodal Model Architecture**\n- Phi-4-multimodal-instruct is a 5.6B parameter multimodal transformer\n- It has separate vision and speech encoders with projectors\n- The vision encoder converts pixel tensors to embedding sequences\n- Uses `VisionAttention` module for non-causal attention in vision encoders\n\n### 3. **LoRA Application to Vision Encoders**\n- When applying LoRA to multimodal models, the system must handle:\n  - Vision encoder forward passes\n  - LoRA weight loading/unloading\n  - Chunked SGMV kernel execution for efficient batching\n\n## Common Causes of Assert Errors\n\nBased on the code structure, potential issues include:\n\n1. **Dimension Mismatches**: The chunked SGMV kernels have strict shape requirements:\n   - Input tensor shape: `(s, num_slices * MAX_RANK)`\n   - Weight tensor shape: `(num_lora, output_dim, MAX_RANK)`\n   - Assert checks: `assert input_dim == num_slices * MAX_RANK`\n\n2. **Vision Encoder Specifics**:\n   - Vision encoders don't maintain KV cache (full self-attention each pass)\n   - Different models use different attention backends (Triton, SDPA, FlashAttention3, etc.)\n   - Patch merging and projection dimensions must align with LoRA ranks\n\n3. **Multimodal Data Processing**:\n   - `MultimodalDataItem` and `MultimodalInputs` structures manage vision data\n   - Feature extraction happens asynchronously before model forward pass\n   - Pad values and token padding patterns must be correctly configured\n\n## Recommended Solutions\n\n### 1. **Check LoRA Configuration**\n```bash\n# Ensure proper LoRA parameters\npython -m sglang.launch_server \\\n    --model-path microsoft/Phi-4-multimodal-instruct \\\n    --enable-lora \\\n    --lora-backend csgmv \\\n    --max-lora-rank <your_rank> \\\n    --lora-target-modules all  # or specific modules\n```\n\n### 2. **Adjust Chunk Size**\nIf encountering performance or assertion issues, try tuning:\n```bash\n--max-lora-chunk-size 8  # or 32, depending on your hardware\n```\n\n### 3. **Vision Encoder Considerations**\n- Ensure LoRA is applied only to supported modules in the vision encoder\n- Check that vision encoder dimensions match expected LoRA shapes\n- Consider using `--mm-enable-dp-encoder` for data-parallel vision encoding\n\n### 4. **Alternative Backend**\nIf issues persist, switch to Triton backend:\n```bash\n--lora-backend triton\n```\n\n## Additional Resources\n\n- **SGLang LoRA Documentation**: https://docs.sglang.io/docs/advanced_features/lora\n- **Phi-4-Multimodal Model Card**: https://huggingface.co/microsoft/Phi-4-multimodal-instruct\n- **Vision-Language Model Architecture**: https://deepwiki.com/sgl-project/sglang/18.1-vision-language-model-architecture\n\n## Reporting the Issue\n\nIf you continue experiencing this error, consider:\n1. Checking SGLang GitHub issues for similar reports\n2. Providing full error traceback and configuration\n3. Testing with different `max_lora_chunk_size` values\n4. Verifying LoRA adapter compatibility with Phi-4-mm architecture\n\nThe error likely stems from dimension mismatches between the LoRA adapter configuration and the vision encoder's expected input/output shapes when using the chunked SGMV optimization.","type":"text"}],"id":"96cdec8a422648139d11ceb22f483988","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":101432,"input_tokens":8867,"output_tokens":978}}
