2026-06-01T14:12:12.073600Z  INFO ThreadId(13) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, I can provide you with a comprehensive explanation of the Phi-4-multimodal speech-LoRA architecture.\n\n## Phi-4-Multimodal Speech-LoRA Architecture\n\n### Overview\nPhi-4-Multimodal is a 5.6B parameter unified multimodal model that processes text, images, and audio/speech inputs through a single neural network. Its key innovation is the **\"Mixture of LoRAs\"** technique, which enables multimodal capabilities while keeping the base language model frozen.\n\n### Core Architecture Components\n\n#### 1. **Base Language Model**\n- **Phi-4-Mini**: 3.8B parameter decoder-only Transformer\n- 32 layers, 3072 hidden dimensions, 24 attention heads, 8 KV heads\n- 200K token vocabulary (expanded from Phi-3.5)\n- Group Query Attention (GQA) for efficient long-context generation\n- 128K context length using LongRoPE\n\n#### 2. **Audio Encoder (Cascades Conformer)**\nThe speech/audio modality uses a specialized audio encoder:\n- **Structure**: 3 convolutional layers + 24 Conformer blocks\n- **Dimensions**: 1024 attention dimensions, 1536 feed-forward dimensions, 16 attention heads\n- **Subsampling**: 8x reduction (80ms token rate) via depthwise separable convolutions\n- **Initialization**: Pre-trained from an attention-based encoder-decoder (AED) ASR model\n- **Parameters**: 460M parameters\n\n#### 3. **Audio Projection Layer**\n- **Type**: 2-layer MLP\n- **Function**: Maps 1024-dim speech features to 3072-dim text embedding space\n- **Parameters**: Part of the 460M audio encoder+projector total\n\n#### 4. **Speech LoRA Adapter**\n- **Rank**: 320\n- **Application**: Applied to all attention and MLP layers in the language decoder\n- **Parameters**: 460M parameters\n- **Purpose**: Adapts the frozen language model for speech/audio tasks without modifying base weights\n\n### How the Speech-LoRA Works\n\n#### **Dynamic Weight Switching**\nThe model uses a sophisticated LoRA management system:\n\n1. **Base Weights Storage**: Original Phi-4-Mini weights stored separately\n2. **LoRA Delta Storage**: Speech LoRA and Vision LoRA stored as delta weights\n3. **Runtime Application**: The `set_modality()` method applies the correct weight combination:\n   - `apply_speech_lora()`: Base + Speech delta\n   - `apply_vision_lora()`: Base + Vision delta  \n   - `apply_both_loras()`: Base + Speech + Vision deltas\n   - `apply_base_weights()`: Text-only mode\n\n#### **Training Pipeline**\nThe speech/audio training follows a two-stage paradigm:\n\n**Stage 1: Pre-training (50k steps)**\n- Freeze language decoder\n- Train audio encoder and projector with learning rate 4e-5\n- Use ~2M hours of speech-text pairs for semantic alignment\n- Result: Model can perform ASR only\n\n**Stage 2: Post-training (50k steps)**\n- Freeze audio encoder\n- Train audio projector and Speech LoRA with learning rate 1e-4\n- Use ~100M curated speech/audio SFT samples\n- Supports various tasks: ASR, AST, SQA, SQQA, speech summarization, audio understanding\n\n### adapter_model.safetensors Structure\n\nThe `adapter_model.safetensors` file contains:\n- **Speech LoRA weights**: Low-rank decomposition matrices (rank 320) for all linear layers\n- **Audio projector weights**: 2-layer MLP parameters\n- **Potentially audio encoder weights**: If not fully frozen during certain training stages\n\n### Key Advantages\n\n1. **Modularity**: New modalities can be added via additional LoRAs without retraining the base model\n2. **Performance Preservation**: Language capabilities remain intact since base model is frozen\n3. **Efficiency**: Only 460M additional parameters for speech modality (vs. full fine-tuning)\n4. **State-of-the-Art Results**: Ranks #1 on OpenASR leaderboard with 6.14% WER\n\n### File Organization\nIn the Hugging Face repository, you'll find:\n```\nmicrosoft/Phi-4-multimodal-instruct/\n├── speech-lora/\n│   └── adapter_model.safetensors  # Speech LoRA weights\n├── vision-lora/\n│   └── adapter_model.safetensors  # Vision LoRA weights\n└── [base model files]\n```\n\nThis architecture represents a significant advancement in efficient multimodal AI, demonstrating that compact models can achieve state-of-the-art performance across multiple modalities through clever parameter-efficient fine-tuning techniques.\n\n**Sources:**\n- [Phi-4-Multimodal Hugging Face Model Card](https://huggingface.co/microsoft/Phi-4-multimodal-instruct)\n- [Phi-4-Mini Technical Report (arXiv:2503.01743)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.01743)\n- [MLX-VLM Phi4-Multimodal Implementation](https://deepwiki.com/Blaizzy/mlx-vlm/3.5-phi4-multimodal)","type":"text"}],"id":"1d4f1b43a21f4fa0bddc179f6b4a0d9b","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":68260,"input_tokens":34202,"output_tokens":1190}}
