2026-06-01T16:20:42.983922Z  INFO ThreadId(10) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, I can now provide a comprehensive answer about SGLang HiCache's hierarchical cache system and its compatibility limitations with multimodal models and LoRA.\n\n## SGLang HiCache: Hierarchical Cache and Compatibility Limitations\n\n### HiCache Overview\n\nSGLang HiCache extends the traditional RadixAttention with a **three-tier hierarchical KV caching system** that dramatically improves performance for long-context and multi-turn conversation scenarios. The hierarchy consists of:\n\n- **L1 (GPU Memory)**: Private to each inference instance, fastest access\n- **L2 (Host/CPU Memory)**: Private buffer between GPU and remote storage  \n- **L3 (Distributed Storage)**: Shared across all inference instances in the cluster (Mooncake, HF3FS, NIXL, AIBrix, etc.)\n\nThis design addresses the fundamental capacity bottleneck that limits cache hit rates in conventional systems by intelligently managing KV caches across GPU memory, host memory, and external storage backends.\n\n### Multimodal Model Limitations\n\n**Current Status**: HiCache **does work with multimodal models** (Vision-Language Models), but with important considerations:\n\n1. **Multimodal Feature Handling**: \n   - By default, multimodal feature tensors are moved to CPU after processing to save GPU memory\n   - The `--keep-mm-feature-on-device` flag can keep features on GPU for lower latency at the cost of higher memory usage\n\n2. **Bidirectional Attention Constraints**:\n   - Models like Gemma-3 that use bidirectional attention between image tokens during prefill are only compatible with the Triton attention backend\n   - This configuration requires disabling CUDA Graph and Chunked Prefill, which can impact performance\n\n3. **Video Processing**:\n   - HiCache supports video inputs for VLMs, but the system samples frames and processes them through the encoder\n   - Large multimodal embeddings from Vision Transformers can be transferred via zero-copy RDMA when using Mooncake backend\n\n### LoRA Compatibility Limitations\n\n**Critical Finding**: **HiCache and LoRA are currently incompatible** when used together.\n\nThe SGLang documentation explicitly states:\n\n> \"Note: HiCache is not compatible with LoRA. If you need to use LoRA, you must disable HiCache.\"\n\nThis limitation exists because:\n- LoRA adapters modify the model weights dynamically during inference\n- HiCache's KV cache reuse assumes static model weights across requests\n- The interaction between dynamic LoRA weight modifications and hierarchical cache management creates conflicts that cannot be safely resolved\n\n### Workarounds and Recommendations\n\n1. **For LoRA + HiCache**: Choose one or the other based on your priority:\n   - Use HiCache for maximum KV cache reuse and throughput in multi-turn scenarios\n   - Use LoRA for model personalization/fine-tuning without hierarchical caching\n\n2. **For Multimodal Models**:\n   - HiCache can be enabled with multimodal models\n   - Consider using `--keep-mm-feature-on-device` if you have sufficient GPU memory and need lower latency\n   - For models requiring bidirectional attention, use Triton backend with appropriate flags\n\n3. **Performance Tuning**:\n   - Configure `--hicache-ratio` and `--hicache-size` based on workload characteristics\n   - Use appropriate memory layouts (`page_first`, `page_first_direct`, `layer_first`) based on I/O backend\n   - Select prefetch policies (`best_effort`, `wait_complete`, `timeout`) based on latency vs. cache hit rate requirements\n\n### Sources\n\n- [SGLang HiCache Best Practices](https://docs.sglang.io/docs/advanced_features/hicache_best_practices)\n- [HiCache System Design and Optimization](https://sgl-project.github.io/advanced_features/hicache_design.html)\n- [Multimodal Language Models Documentation](https://docs.sglang.io/docs/supported-models/multimodal_language_models)\n- [SGLang HiCache Integration with Mooncake](https://deepwiki.com/kvcache-ai/Mooncake/7.2-sglang-hicache-integration)","type":"text"}],"id":"cf33da09242541478aaf2822f1ce1e42","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":100415,"output_tokens":850}}
