2026-06-01T16:21:39.228940Z  INFO ThreadId(13) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, I can now provide you with a comprehensive answer about the SGLang HiCache and LoRA incompatibility and KV cache conflicts.\n\n## SGLang HiCache + LoRA Incompatibility: KV Cache Conflict Explanation\n\n### The Core Problem\n\n**HiCache and LoRA are fundamentally incompatible** because they create conflicting requirements for KV cache management:\n\n1. **HiCache** is designed to **reuse and persist KV caches** across requests that share common prefixes, storing them in a three-tier hierarchy (GPU L1 → Host L2 → Distributed Storage L3) to avoid redundant computation.\n\n2. **LoRA** dynamically **modifies model weights** during inference, meaning the same input tokens produce **different KV cache values** depending on which LoRA adapter is active.\n\n### Why the Conflict Occurs\n\nThe conflict stems from **KV cache identity assumptions**:\n\n- **HiCache** assumes that identical token sequences always produce identical KV caches (deterministic computation)\n- **LoRA** breaks this assumption because:\n  - Different LoRA adapters modify attention weights\n  - The same token sequence with different LoRA weights generates different KV values\n  - HiCache cannot safely reuse KV caches across different LoRA configurations\n\n### Evidence from SGLang Issue #24758\n\nA critical bug report ([#24758](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/24758)) demonstrates this problem:\n\n- **Test scenario**: Model A and Model B (same base model with perturbed attention weights) shared the same storage directory and `served_model_name`\n- **Result**: Model B incorrectly loaded KV caches from Model A, producing wrong outputs\n- **Root cause**: Storage page keys are derived **only from token IDs**, not from effective model identity (weights, LoRA, quantization, etc.)\n\nThe issue explicitly lists LoRA as one of the factors that makes KV caches incompatible:\n\n> \"Reusing pages across different base weights, **LoRA adapters/scales**, quantization, TP/CP layout, page size, KV layout, dtype, or attention backend can silently produce incorrect output or crash.\"\n\n### Technical Details\n\n**Storage Key Computation** (from [hicache_storage.py](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/python/sglang/srt/mem_cache/hicache_storage.py)):\n- Keys are computed as: `hash(tokens[i:i+page_size] || prior_hash)`\n- No information about model weights, LoRA identity, or adapter scales is included\n- This means identical token sequences always map to the same storage key regardless of LoRA configuration\n\n**File Backend Naming** (from the issue):\n- Files are named: `{hash}_{served_model_name}_{tp_rank}_{tp_size}.bin`\n- `served_model_name` is just an API alias, not a robust model identity\n- Two different LoRA configurations with the same `served_model_name` would share storage\n\n### Practical Implications\n\n**When HiCache is enabled with LoRA:**\n- KV caches from requests with LoRA adapter A may be incorrectly reused for requests with adapter B\n- This leads to **silent corruption** of outputs (wrong text generation)\n- No error is raised; the system appears to work but produces incorrect results\n\n**Recommended Solutions:**\n\n1. **Disable HiCache when using LoRA**:\n   ```bash\n   # Do NOT use --enable-hierarchical-cache with LoRA\n   python -m sglang.launch_server --model-path ... --lora-path ...\n   ```\n\n2. **Use separate storage namespaces** (if you must use both):\n   - Different `served_model_name` for each LoRA configuration\n   - Separate storage directories per LoRA adapter\n   - This is fragile and not recommended\n\n3. **Wait for future fixes**: The SGLang team is aware of this limitation. A proper fix would require:\n   - Including LoRA identity in storage keys\n   - Validating model identity before loading cached KV pages\n   - Potentially maintaining separate cache hierarchies per LoRA configuration\n\n### Current Status\n\nAs of the latest documentation and code, **HiCache and LoRA remain incompatible**. The SGLang documentation does not explicitly mention this limitation, but the codebase and issue tracker confirm the conflict.\n\n**Sources:**\n- [SGLang HiCache Design Documentation](https://docs.sglang.io/docs/advanced_features/hicache_design)\n- [GitHub Issue #24758: HiCache file/L3 storage can reload KV pages across incompatible model identity](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/24758)\n- [SGLang HiCache Best Practices](https://docs.sglang.io/docs/advanced_features/hicache_best_practices)\n- [DeepWiki: HiCache Architecture](https://deepwiki.com/mingfeima/sglang/6.3-hierarchical-cache-(hicache))","type":"text"}],"id":"06d179edd39f4d21aa28b154add36e6a","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":43536,"input_tokens":36353,"output_tokens":1046}}
2026-06-01T16:21:52.721418Z  INFO ThreadId(15) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"I'll search for documentation on SGLang's hicache parameters.\n\n","type":"text"},{"id":"call_0f42039110dc4dc2827e2537","input":{"query":"SGLang hicache-ratio hicache-write-policy hicache-size parameters documentation"},"name":"search","type":"tool_use"}],"id":"4c7c0b3ba0774135ba55fe4dc0966126","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":960,"input_tokens":45,"output_tokens":54}}
2026-06-01T16:22:08.417041Z  INFO ThreadId(15) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my search results, I found comprehensive documentation on SGLang's HiCache parameters. Here's the detailed information:\n\n## SGLang HiCache Parameters Documentation\n\n### Core HiCache Parameters\n\n#### `--hicache-ratio`\n- **Description**: The ratio of the size of host KV cache memory pool to the size of device (GPU) pool.\n- **Example**: A value of 2 means the host memory pool is twice as large as the device memory pool.\n- **Constraint**: Must be greater than 1, as host memory allocated for KV cache must be larger than device memory.\n- **Default**: 2.0\n\n#### `--hicache-size`\n- **Description**: The size of host KV cache memory pool in gigabytes.\n- **Example**: `--hicache-size 30` allocates 30GB (1GB = 1e9 bytes) for the host memory pool **for each rank**. With 8 ranks, total memory is 240GB.\n- **Behavior**: Overrides `hicache-ratio` if set.\n- **Constraint**: Must be larger than the device memory allocated for KV cache.\n- **Default**: 0 (disabled)\n\n#### `--hicache-write-policy`\nControls how data is written from faster to slower memory tiers (L1→L2→L3):\n\n- **`write_through`**: Immediately writes data to all tiers. Provides strongest caching benefits when bandwidth is sufficient.\n- **`write_through_selective`**: Uses hit-count tracking to back up only frequently accessed data. Reduces I/O overhead.\n- **`write_back`**: Writes data back to slower tiers only when eviction is needed. Reduces I/O load and alleviates storage pressure.\n- **Default**: `write_through_selective`\n\n### Related Important Parameters\n\n#### `--enable-hierarchical-cache`\n- **Required**: Must be enabled to use HiCache functionality.\n- **Type**: Boolean flag\n\n#### `--page-size`\n- **Description**: Number of tokens per page. Determines granularity of KV cache storage and retrieval.\n- **Trade-offs**: Larger page sizes reduce metadata overhead and improve I/O efficiency but may lower cache hit rate when only part of a page matches.\n- **Default**: Varies (commonly 64)\n\n#### `--hicache-storage-prefetch-policy`\nControls when prefetching from L3 storage should stop:\n\n- **`best_effort`**: Prefetch as much as possible without blocking. Suitable for latency-sensitive scenarios.\n- **`wait_complete`**: Wait for prefetch to complete before proceeding. Suitable for high cache hit rate requirements.\n- **`timeout`**: Terminates after specified time or when complete. Recommended for production environments to meet SLOs.\n- **Default**: `best_effort`\n\n#### `--hicache-io-backend`\nChoose I/O backend for CPU↔GPU transfers:\n\n- **`direct`**: Standard CUDA memory copy operations\n- **`kernel`**: GPU-assisted I/O kernels (recommended for better performance, up to 3x faster)\n- **Default**: `kernel`\n\n#### `--hicache-mem-layout`\nMemory layout for host memory pool:\n\n- **`layer_first`**: Compatible with GPU computation kernels (default for GPU memory)\n- **`page_first`**: Optimized for I/O efficiency (only compatible with `kernel` backend)\n- **`page_first_direct`**: Groups all tokens of a given layer within a page, allowing aggregated transfers (compatible with `direct` backend)\n- **Default**: `layer_first`\n\n#### `--hicache-storage-backend`\nChoose storage backend for L3 tier:\n\n- **Built-in options**: `file`, `mooncake`, `hf3fs`, `nixl`, `aibrix`, `dynamic`\n- **Default**: None (L3 disabled)\n\n### Performance Notes\n\n- **`--hicache-ratio` and `--hicache-size` are critical parameters**. Larger HiCache size generally leads to higher cache hit rates and better prefill performance, but the relationship is not linear—diminishing returns occur once most reusable KV data is cached.\n- **Write policy selection**: `write_through` provides strongest caching if bandwidth permits; `write_through_selective` balances I/O load; `write_back` maximizes GPU utilization when storage is limited.\n- **Prefetch tuning**: Use `timeout` policy for production with appropriate `prefetch_timeout_base` and `prefetch_timeout_per_ki_token` parameters.\n\n### Example Configuration\n\n```bash\npython3 -m sglang.launch_server \\\n  --model-path /path/to/model \\\n  --enable-hierarchical-cache \\\n  --hicache-ratio 2 \\\n  --hicache-write-policy write_through \\\n  --hicache-io-backend kernel \\\n  --hicache-mem-layout page_first \\\n  --hicache-storage-backend mooncake \\\n  --hicache-storage-prefetch-policy timeout \\\n  --page-size 64\n```\n\n**Sources:**\n- [SGLang HiCache Design Documentation](https://docs.sglang.io/docs/advanced_features/hicache_design)\n- [SGLang HiCache Best Practices](https://sgl-project.github.io/advanced_features/hicache_best_practices.html)\n- [SGLang HiCache Blog Post](https://www.lmsys.org/blog/2025-09-10-sglang-hicache/)","type":"text"}],"id":"94f6b686aa754af19d64491c6f28e34a","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":29624,"output_tokens":1165}}
