2026-06-01T16:23:02.654416Z  INFO ThreadId(11) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, I can provide you with comprehensive information about Phi-4-multimodal inference with SGLang, focusing on memory offloading and CPU/GPU considerations.\n\n## Phi-4-Multimodal Support in SGLang\n\nPhi-4-multimodal-instruct is officially supported in SGLang as a multimodal model that handles text, vision, and audio modalities. The model is based on Phi-4-mini with LoRA adapters for vision and speech capabilities.\n\n## Memory Offloading and CPU/GPU Considerations\n\n### 1. **Multimodal Feature Tensor Management**\n\nSGLang provides a critical flag for managing multimodal feature memory:\n\n**`--keep-mm-feature-on-device`**\n\n- **Default behavior (False)**: Multimodal feature tensors are moved to CPU after processing to save GPU memory\n- **With flag enabled (True)**: Feature tensors remain on GPU, reducing device-to-host copy overhead and improving latency, but consuming more GPU memory\n\n**Use case**: Enable this flag when you have sufficient GPU memory and want to minimize latency for multimodal inference.\n\n### 2. **Hierarchical KV Cache (HiCache)**\n\nFor long-context scenarios and multi-turn conversations, SGLang's HiCache system provides three-tier memory management:\n\n**Core HiCache Parameters:**\n```bash\n--enable-hierarchical-cache           # Enable HiCache\n--hicache-ratio 2                     # Host memory ratio (2x GPU memory)\n--hicache-size 100                    # Host memory size in GBs\n--hicache-io-backend kernel           # I/O backend for CPU-GPU transfers\n--hicache-write-policy write_through  # Cache write policy\n--hicache-storage-backend             # Optional external storage (hf3fs, mooncake, etc.)\n```\n\n**Memory Layout Options:**\n- `page_first`: Optimized for I/O efficiency with zero-copy (recommended with kernel backend)\n- `page_first_direct`: Optimized for direct I/O operations (compatible with FA3)\n- `layer_first`: Traditional layout\n\n### 3. **Multimodal Input Processing Configuration**\n\nTo manage GPU memory usage for multimodal inputs:\n\n**`--mm-process-config`**\n```bash\n--mm-process-config '{\"image\":{\"max_pixels\":1048576},\"video\":{\"fps\":3,\"max_pixels\":602112,\"max_frames\":60}}'\n```\n\nThis allows you to set limits on image, video, and audio inputs to:\n- Reduce GPU memory usage\n- Improve inference speed\n- Avoid OOM errors\n- Trade off some model performance for efficiency\n\n### 4. **Additional Multimodal Optimization Flags**\n\n- **`--mm_max_concurrent_calls`** (default: 32): Maximum parallel multimodal processing tasks\n- **`--mm_per_request_timeout`** (default: 10.0s): Timeout per multimodal request\n- **`--mm_enable_dp_encoder`**: Enable data parallelism for encoder across GPUs\n- **`--enable_broadcast_mm_inputs_process`**: Broadcast processed features in DP/TP scenarios\n\n### 5. **Tensor Transport Modes**\n\nSGLang automatically determines optimal tensor transport:\n- **CUDA IPC**: Used for single-node deployments (fastest, zero-copy)\n- **CPU memory + pickle**: Used for multi-node deployments (slower but necessary)\n\n## Performance Considerations\n\n### Memory vs. Latency Trade-offs\n\n1. **GPU Memory Optimization**:\n   - Keep `--keep-mm-feature-on-device=False` (default) to offload features to CPU\n   - Use HiCache with appropriate ratio to extend effective memory\n   - Set reasonable `--mm-process-config` limits\n\n2. **Latency Optimization**:\n   - Enable `--keep-mm-feature-on-device=True` if GPU memory permits\n   - Use HiCache with `page_first_direct` layout and `kernel` I/O backend\n   - Increase `--mm_max_concurrent_calls` for higher throughput\n\n### HiCache Performance Benefits\n\nAccording to SGLang benchmarks, HiCache can achieve:\n- Up to 6× throughput improvement\n- Up to 80% reduction in Time-To-First-Token (TTFT)\n- 84% reduction in TTFT for cache hits compared to full re-computation\n\n## Example Deployment Command\n\n```bash\npython3 -m sglang.launch_server \\\n  --model-path microsoft/Phi-4-multimodal-instruct \\\n  --host 0.0.0.0 \\\n  --port 30000 \\\n  --enable-multimodal \\\n  --keep-mm-feature-on-device True \\\n  --enable-hierarchical-cache \\\n  --hicache-ratio 2 \\\n  --hicache-io-backend kernel \\\n  --hicache-mem-layout page_first_direct \\\n  --mm-process-config '{\"image\":{\"max_pixels\":1048576},\"video\":{\"fps\":3,\"max_frames\":60}}' \\\n  --mm_max_concurrent_calls 64\n```\n\n## Key Recommendations\n\n1. **For memory-constrained environments**: Use default feature offloading and configure HiCache with appropriate storage backend\n2. **For latency-sensitive applications**: Keep features on GPU and optimize HiCache I/O backend\n3. **For long-context scenarios**: Enable HiCache with external storage backend (Mooncake, 3FS, etc.)\n4. **Monitor GPU memory**: Use `--enable-cache-report` to track cache utilization\n\nThe combination of these features allows SGLang to efficiently serve Phi-4-multimodal across a wide range of hardware configurations, from single GPU setups to large distributed clusters.\n\n**Sources:**\n- SGLang Multimodal Language Models Documentation: https://docs.sglang.io/docs/supported-models/multimodal_language_models\n- SGLang HiCache Best Practices: https://docs.sglang.io/docs/advanced_features/hicache_best_practices\n- SGLang GitHub Repository: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang","type":"text"}],"id":"6b6049fc18ad41b6a67da40f198ec25e","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":44508,"input_tokens":27823,"output_tokens":1276}}
