2026-06-01T16:45:53.693565Z  INFO ThreadId(13) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, here's a comprehensive summary of the latest updates on SGLang's Mamba2 hybrid support and Nemotron Omni for 2026:\n\n## SGLang Mamba2 Hybrid Support\n\nSGLang has implemented comprehensive support for hybrid Mamba-Transformer architectures, addressing the unique challenges these models present:\n\n### Key Technical Innovations:\n\n**Memory Management**\n- Separated memory pools: Mamba pool (for linear layers) and KV cache pool (for attention layers)\n- Elastic memory pool that dynamically adjusts pool ratios based on workload demands\n- Request-level state storage for Mamba states with `HybridReqToTokenPool` binding\n\n**Prefix Caching**\n- Implemented `MambaRadixCache` to enable prefix caching for hybrid models\n- Handles in-place state updates and large state sizes\n- Maintains separate LRU lists for Mamba states and KV cache\n\n**Speculative Decoding**\n- Each draft token receives a private cache slot with its own SSM state\n- Supports EAGLE-Tree with Top-K > 1 through parent index precomputation\n\n**Prefill-Decode Disaggregation**\n- Extended transfer protocol with dedicated state transfer channel\n- Transmits Mamba conv/temporal states and sliding window states atomically\n- Supports multiple state types (Mamba, SWA, NSA)\n\n## Nemotron Omni 2026 Updates\n\nNVIDIA has released **Nemotron 3 Nano Omni**, a significant advancement in multimodal AI:\n\n### Model Specifications:\n- **Architecture**: 30B total / 3B active parameters hybrid Mamba-Transformer MoE\n- **Modalities**: Native support for text, image, video, and audio in a single model\n- **Context**: 1M token context window (scaled from 16K → 49K → 262K)\n- **Efficiency**: 9x higher throughput than other open omni models\n- **Accuracy**: ~20% higher multimodal intelligence vs best open alternatives\n\n### Key Features:\n- **Unified Architecture**: Single model replaces fragmented multimodal stacks\n- **Vision**: C-RADIOv4-H encoder with 3D convolutions and Efficient Video Sampling (EVS)\n- **Audio**: NVIDIA Parakeet encoder\n- **Quantization**: FP8 and NVFP4 support (NVFP4 requires Blackwell hardware)\n- **Reasoning**: Configurable thinking budget with ON/OFF toggle\n- **Tool Calling**: Native support with `qwen3_coder` parser\n\n### Deployment:\nSGLang provides day-0 support with commands like:\n```bash\nsglang serve --model-path nvidia/Nemotron-3-Nano-Omni-30B-A3B-Reasoning \\\n  --tp 4 --trust-remote-code --tool-call-parser qwen3_coder \\\n  --reasoning-parser deepseek-r1\n```\n\n### Performance Benchmarks (8×B200):\n- Input throughput: 10,080 tok/s\n- Output throughput: 10,107 tok/s  \n- Peak output throughput: 20,199 tok/s\n- Mean TTFT: 220ms\n- GSM8K accuracy: 83.0%\n- MMLU average: 73.7%\n\n### Use Cases:\n- Computer Use Agents (GUI navigation)\n- Document Intelligence\n- Audio & Video Understanding Agents\n- Multi-agent systems with high concurrency\n\nThe integration represents a major step forward in efficient, open multimodal AI, combining SGLang's optimized serving infrastructure with NVIDIA's state-of-the-art hybrid architecture.\n\nSources:\n- [SGLang Documentation - Nemotron 3 Nano Omni](https://docs.sglang.io/cookbook/autoregressive/NVIDIA/Nemotron3-Nano-Omni)\n- [PyTorch Blog - Hybrid Models Meet SGLang](https://pytorch.org/blog/hybrid-models-meet-sglang-more-than-full-attention/)\n- [NVIDIA Nemotron GitHub](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Nemotron)\n- [SGLang GitHub Repository](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang)","type":"text"}],"id":"2fd6223934fe4f6d96324332b0046e2e","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":34296,"input_tokens":17654,"output_tokens":901}}
