2026-06-02T01:03:07.487848Z  INFO ThreadId(11) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on the SGLang documentation, here's a clear comparison between the `/generate` and `/v1/chat/completions` endpoints regarding think tags and reasoning parsing:\n\n## Key Differences\n\n### `/v1/chat/completions` (OpenAI-Compatible API)\n- **Automatic reasoning separation**: When you set `separate_reasoning: true` in the request, the server automatically parses think tags and returns two separate fields:\n  - `reasoning_content`: The chain-of-thought reasoning\n  - `content`: The final answer\n- **No manual parsing required**: The separation happens server-side\n- **Default behavior**: Reasoning separation is enabled by default when a `--reasoning-parser` is specified at server launch\n\nExample:\n```python\nresponse = client.chat.completions.create(\n    model=model_name,\n    messages=messages,\n    extra_body={\"separate_reasoning\": True},\n)\n# Returns response.choices[0].message.reasoning_content and .content\n```\n\n### `/generate` (SGLang Native API)\n- **Raw output**: Returns the complete model output with think tags intact (e.g., `<think>...</think>`)\n- **Manual parsing required**: You must separately call the `/separate_reasoning` endpoint or use the `ReasoningParser` class to extract reasoning from the raw text\n- **Two-step process**: First generate, then parse\n\nExample:\n```python\n# Step 1: Generate raw output\ngen_response = requests.post(gen_url, json=gen_data).json()[\"text\"]\n\n# Step 2: Parse separately\nparse_response = requests.post(parse_url, json={\n    \"text\": gen_response,\n    \"reasoning_parser\": \"deepseek-r1\",\n}).json()\n# Returns reasoning_text and text\n```\n\n## Think Tags Handling\n\nBoth endpoints use the same underlying reasoning parsers (e.g., `deepseek-r1`, `qwen3`, `kimi_k2`) that recognize model-specific think tag formats:\n\n| Model | Think Tags |\n|-------|------------|\n| DeepSeek-R1 | `<think>` … `</think>` (or no start tag) |\n| DeepSeek-V3 | `<think>` … `</think>` |\n| Qwen3 | `<think>` … `</think>` |\n| Kimi K2 | `◁think▷` … `◁/think▷` |\n| GPT OSS | `<\\|channel\\|>analysis<\\|message\\|>` … `<\\|end\\|>` |\n\nThe parser is specified at server launch with `--reasoning-parser` and applies to both endpoints.\n\n## When to Use Which\n\n- Use `/v1/chat/completions` when you want a simple, OpenAI-like interface with automatic reasoning separation\n- Use `/generate` when you need the raw model output or want to implement custom parsing logic\n\nSources:\n- [SGLang Reasoning Parser Documentation](https://docs.sglang.io/docs/advanced_features/separate_reasoning)\n- [SGLang GitHub Repository - separate_reasoning.mdx](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/docs_new/docs/advanced_features/separate_reasoning.mdx)","type":"text"}],"id":"eaa50d7b37f0471fae797fc6c3c9c674","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":22773,"output_tokens":680}}
