2026-06-02T01:03:34.135478Z  INFO ThreadId(13) universal_search_service::service: 683: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, I can now provide you with a comprehensive answer about the \"SGLang\" \"nemotron\" \"reasoning_content\" \"content\" leak issue.\n\n## Summary\n\nThere is **no evidence of a data leak** specifically involving `reasoning_content` and `content` fields in SGLang with Nemotron models. However, there are **critical security vulnerabilities** in SGLang that could potentially lead to data exposure or unauthorized access.\n\n## Key Findings\n\n### 1. **Critical SGLang Vulnerabilities (CVE-2026-5760 and Others)**\n\nSGLang has multiple critical security vulnerabilities that could compromise systems:\n\n- **CVE-2026-5760** (CVSS 9.8): Server-side template injection (SSTI) vulnerability in the `/v1/rerank` endpoint that allows arbitrary code execution through malicious GGUF model files\n- **CVE-2026-3059 & CVE-2026-3060** (CVSS 9.8): Remote code execution via unsafe pickle deserialization in ZMQ broker\n- **CVE-2026-3989** (CVSS 7.8): Local code execution through crash dump replay utility\n\n### 2. **Nemotron Integration with SGLang**\n\nNVIDIA Nemotron models are designed to work with SGLang and properly expose reasoning content through the OpenAI-compatible API:\n\n```python\nresp = client.chat.completions.create(\n    model=\"nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3-Super-120B-A12B-BF16\",\n    messages=[...],\n    temperature=0.6,\n    max_tokens=1024,\n)\nprint(\"Reasoning:\", resp.choices[0].message.reasoning_content)\nprint(\"Content:\", resp.choices[0].message.content)\n```\n\nThis is **intended functionality**, not a leak. Nemotron models are specifically designed to output both reasoning traces and final responses.\n\n### 3. **Security Risks**\n\nThe vulnerabilities in SGLang could potentially allow attackers to:\n- Execute arbitrary code on servers running SGLang\n- Access sensitive data including model weights, API keys, and inference data\n- Compromise entire GPU clusters\n\n### 4. **Current Status**\n\n- **No official patches** are available for CVE-2026-5760\n- SGLang maintainers have been **non-responsive** to coordinated disclosure efforts through CERT/CC\n- Organizations are advised to:\n  - Disable the `/v1/rerank` endpoint if not needed\n  - Apply network segmentation\n  - Audit GGUF model file sources\n  - Upgrade to SGLang 0.5.10+ for ZMQ vulnerabilities\n\n## Sources\n\n1. [CERT/CC Vulnerability Note VU#915947](https://kb.cert.org/vuls/id/915947)\n2. [Orca Security Research on SGLang RCE Vulnerabilities](https://orca.security/resources/blog/sglang-llm-framework-rce-vulnerabilities/)\n3. [Cloud Security Alliance Research on CVE-2026-5760](https://labs.cloudsecurityalliance.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/CSA_research_note_sglang-cve-2026-5760-llm-serving-rce_20260421-csa-styled.pdf)\n4. [SGLang Documentation for Nemotron](https://docs.sglang.io/cookbook/autoregressive/NVIDIA/Nemotron3-Super)\n\nThe term \"leak\" in your query likely refers to these security vulnerabilities rather than an actual data leak of reasoning content, which is an intentional feature of Nemotron models.","type":"text"}],"id":"41542024db4f45a2afb3c0870f056e9e","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":960,"input_tokens":70798,"output_tokens":831}}
