2026-06-02T17:17:16.612751Z  INFO ThreadId(16) universal_search_service::service: 685: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, here's a comprehensive guide to **Unsloth GGUF inference, serving, model loading, and PyTorch integration**:\n\n## Unsloth GGUF Workflow Overview\n\nUnsloth provides a seamless pipeline from fine-tuning to GGUF deployment:\n\n### 1. **Exporting Models to GGUF Format**\n\nAfter fine-tuning with Unsloth, you can export your model to GGUF format:\n\n```python\n# Direct GGUF export (recommended)\nmodel.save_pretrained_gguf(\"directory\", tokenizer, quantization_method=\"q4_k_m\")\n\n# Or push directly to Hugging Face Hub\nmodel.push_to_hub_gguf(\"username/repo\", tokenizer, quantization_method=\"q4_k_m\")\n```\n\n**Supported quantization methods** include:\n- `q4_k_m` (recommended, best balance)\n- `q5_k_m`, `q6_k`, `q8_0`\n- `f16`, `f32` (full precision)\n- `iq3_xs`, `iq2_xs` (for extreme compression)\n\n### 2. **Model Loading and Inference**\n\n#### **Using Unsloth for PyTorch Inference**\n```python\nfrom unsloth import FastLanguageModel\n\n# Load model for inference\nmodel, tokenizer = FastLanguageModel.from_pretrained(\n    model_name=\"your_model\",\n    max_seq_length=2048,\n    load_in_4bit=True  # or False for full precision\n)\n\n# Enable optimized inference\nFastLanguageModel.for_inference(model)\n\n# Generate text\ninputs = tokenizer(\"Your prompt\", return_tensors=\"pt\").to(\"cuda\")\noutputs = model.generate(**inputs, max_new_tokens=256)\n```\n\n#### **Using GGUF with llama.cpp**\nFor CPU/edge deployment, convert to GGUF and use llama.cpp:\n\n```bash\n# Using llama-server for OpenAI-compatible API\n./llama-server -m model.gguf -ngl 99 --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8080\n\n# Or use llama-cli for direct inference\n./llama-cli -m model.gguf -p \"Your prompt\" -n 256\n```\n\n### 3. **Serving Models**\n\n#### **vLLM Deployment (GPU)**\n```python\n# Export to float16 first\nmodel.save_pretrained_merged(\"merged_model\", tokenizer, save_method=\"merged_16bit\")\n\n# Then serve with vLLM\nfrom vllm import LLM\nllm = LLM(model=\"merged_model\")\n```\n\n#### **llama.cpp Server (CPU/GPU)**\n```bash\n# Start server with GGUF model\npython -m llama_cpp.server --model model.gguf --n_gpu_layers 35\n```\n\n### 4. **Advanced: llcuda for Multi-GPU Deployment**\n\nFor Kaggle dual T4 GPUs or multi-GPU setups, use **llcuda**:\n\n```python\nfrom llcuda.server import ServerManager, ServerConfig\n\nconfig = ServerConfig(\n    model_path=\"model.gguf\",\n    n_gpu_layers=99,\n    tensor_split=\"0.5,0.5\",  # Use both GPUs\n    flash_attn=True\n)\n\nserver = ServerManager()\nserver.start_with_config(config)\n# Server now available at http://localhost:8080 with OpenAI API\n```\n\n## Key Considerations\n\n1. **Chat Templates**: When exporting, ensure you use the same chat template that was used during training to avoid gibberish outputs.\n\n2. **Memory Optimization**: During export, reduce `maximum_memory_usage` (default 0.75) to 0.5 if encountering OOM errors.\n\n3. **Performance**: \n   - GGUF with Q4_K_M offers ~75% size reduction with good quality\n   - vLLM provides fastest GPU inference\n   - llama.cpp enables CPU/edge deployment\n\n4. **PyTorch Integration**: Unsloth models work directly with PyTorch and transformers, with 2x faster inference when using `FastLanguageModel.for_inference()`.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Unsloth GGUF Documentation](https://unsloth.ai/docs/basics/inference-and-deployment/saving-to-gguf)\n- [Unsloth Model Export Guide](https://deepwiki.com/unslothai/notebooks/5.2-model-export-and-deployment)\n- [llcuda Inference Backend](https://llcuda.github.io/)","type":"text"}],"id":"8dfc60c19a4e44719c0d78ab848fe1a1","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":42552,"input_tokens":9599,"output_tokens":969}}
