2026-06-03T00:58:46.640655Z  INFO ThreadId(11) universal_search_service::service: 685: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my search of the `ggml-org/llama.cpp` repository, here's what I found regarding **nemotron**:\n\n## Nemotron Support in llama.cpp\n\nllama.cpp has support for NVIDIA's Nemotron models. Here are the key findings:\n\n### 1. **Nemotron 3 Models** (Latest)\nThe repository includes performance benchmarks and support for the **NVIDIA Nemotron 3** family:\n- **NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Super 120B**: A 120B parameter mixture-of-experts (MoE) model with 12B active parameters, featuring a hybrid Transformer-Mamba architecture and up to 1M context window\n- **NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Nano 4B**: A compact 4B parameter model with Mamba2-Transformer hybrid architecture and up to 262k context\n\nPerformance benchmarks for these models are available in the repository at `benches/nemotron/nemotron-dgx-spark.md`.\n\n### 2. **Llama-3.1-Nemotron Models**\nThere's also support for **Llama-3.1-Nemotron-51B**, which is a modified Llama architecture with:\n- Variable query attention layers\n- Linear attention layers\n- Attention-free layers\n\nA community member created a fork to support this model, and GGUF conversions are available on Hugging Face.\n\n### 3. **Model Availability**\nGGUF format models for Nemotron are available on Hugging Face:\n- [NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Super 120B GGUF](https://huggingface.co/ggml-org/Nemotron-3-Super-120B-GGUF)\n- [NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Nano 4B GGUF](https://huggingface.co/ggml-org/Nemotron-3-Nano-4B-GGUF)\n\n### Sources\n- Performance discussion: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/discussions/20421\n- Benchmarks directory: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/tree/master/benches/nemotron\n- Feature request for Llama-3.1-Nemotron-51: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/10648\n- Community discussion about Nemotron models: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/discussions/7954","type":"text"}],"id