2026-06-03T01:03:08.265415Z  INFO ThreadId(17) universal_search_service::service: 685: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, I can provide you with comprehensive information about llama.cpp's Mamba architecture support.\n\n## llama.cpp Mamba Architecture Support\n\n**Yes, llama.cpp fully supports Mamba architecture.** Here are the key details:\n\n### Supported Mamba Variants\nllama.cpp supports both **Mamba** and **Mamba2** architectures through dedicated implementations:\n- `LLM_ARCH_MAMBA` for standard Mamba models (e.g., Mamba-130M, Mamba-2.8B)\n- `LLM_ARCH_MAMBA2` for Mamba2 variants\n\n### Implementation Details\nThe Mamba support includes:\n\n1. **Selective Scan Mechanism**: Mamba models use a selective scan mechanism with hyperparameters like:\n   - `ssm_d_conv` (convolution dimension)\n   - `ssm_d_inner` (inner dimension)\n   - `ssm_d_state` (state dimension)\n\n2. **Memory Management**: Mamba models use `llama_memory_recurrent` for state handling, which differs from the KV cache used in transformer models.\n\n3. **Model Files**: Implementation is located in:\n   - `src/models/mamba.cpp` and `src/models/mamba2.cpp`\n   - Architecture definitions in `src/llama-arch.cpp` and `src/llama-arch.h`\n\n### Hybrid Mamba Models\nllama.cpp also supports **hybrid Mamba2 architectures** that combine Mamba2 layers with attention layers. This includes models like:\n- **Bamba-9B** (IBM's hybrid Mamba2 model)\n- **Falcon Mamba** and **Falcon 3 Mamba**\n- **Zamba** (with shared attention layers)\n\n### Recent Developments\nThe Bamba project (December 2024) specifically enabled hybrid Mamba2 architecture in llama.cpp, along with other frameworks like transformers, vLLM, and TRL. This demonstrates active community support and ongoing improvements.\n\n### Usage\nMamba models can be used with llama.cpp just like any other supported architecture:\n```bash\nllama-cli -m mamba_model.gguf\nllama-server -m mamba_model.gguf\n```\n\n### Performance Benefits\nMamba architectures offer significant inference efficiency improvements over standard transformers:\n- Up to 2.5x better throughput\n- 2x latency improvements\n- Potential 5x speedup in memory-bound scenarios\n- Constant KV-cache size (solves the KV-cache bottleneck)\n\n### Sources\n- [llama.cpp Supported Model Architectures](https://deepwiki.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/3.11-supported-model-architectures)\n- [llama.cpp GitHub Repository](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp)\n- [Bamba: Inference-Efficient Hybrid Mamba2 Model](https://huggingface.co/blog/bamba)\n\nThe support is mature and actively maintained, making llama.cpp one of the primary inference engines for Mamba-based models.","type":"text"}],"id":"d54a43f0da504c829edca207ba6f0c95","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":51731,"output_tokens":644}}
