2026-06-03T02:22:31.024766Z  INFO ThreadId(11) universal_search_service::service: 685: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"I'll search for research papers that combine dual quaternions with machine learning, specifically focusing on dimensionality reduction and encoder-decoder architectures.\n\n","type":"text"},{"id":"call_807029b761374e04ad2391e0","input":{"query":"dual quaternion machine learning dimensionality reduction encoder decoder"},"name":"search","type":"tool_use"}],"id":"b006bfc920f94470bd83d842237a60e2","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":960,"input_tokens":40,"output_tokens":62}}
2026-06-03T02:22:43.403133Z  INFO ThreadId(11) universal_search_service::service: 685: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Let me search more specifically for dual quaternion applications in machine learning and neural networks:\n\n","type":"text"},{"id":"call_bddfdd9ddc0f4860b41681a6","input":{"query":"dual quaternion neural network machine learning"},"name":"search","type":"tool_use"}],"id":"2699c94997d24933ba9fe850839fea0d","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":23298,"output_tokens":47}}
2026-06-03T02:22:50.479274Z  INFO ThreadId(11) universal_search_service::service: 685: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Let me search for more specific information about dual quaternion applications in dimensionality reduction and autoencoders:\n\n","type":"text"},{"id":"call_1fb2b0243bab4c92ae863ad6","input":{"query":"dual quaternion autoencoder dimensionality reduction"},"name":"search","type":"tool_use"}],"id":"fcc4c0ea60a64baaab42b90b09e88354","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":23344,"input_tokens":44809,"output_tokens":52}}
2026-06-03T02:23:08.312399Z  INFO ThreadId(11) universal_search_service::service: 685: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, I can provide you with information about papers that combine dual quaternions with machine learning, particularly focusing on dimensionality reduction and encoder-decoder architectures.\n\n## Key Papers on Dual Quaternion Machine Learning with Encoder-Decoder Architectures\n\n### 1. **Neural Net Based Dual Quaternion Stochastic Filtering for Relative Spacecraft Motion Estimation**\n- **Authors:** Warren Soh & Regina Lee (2026)\n- **Published in:** Journal of the Astronautical Sciences\n- **Key Contribution:** This paper introduces a **Dual-Quaternion Multiplicative Extended Kalman Filter with Neural Network (DQ-MEKF-NN)** architecture that integrates physics-informed neural networks with dual quaternion filtering.\n- **Architecture Details:**\n  - Uses dual quaternions to represent 6-DOF rigid body motion (rotation + translation)\n  - Employs two lightweight neural networks operating in parallel:\n    - **Translation Network:** Three-layer fully connected network with tanh activations\n    - **Attitude Network:** Radial basis function (RBF) network with unit-norm quaternion output\n  - Both networks use an encoder-decoder-like structure where the networks recursively ingest pose measurements and reformulated dual-quaternion states\n  - Implements online learning with composite data-driven and kinematic consistency losses\n- **Results:** Achieves up to 97% reduction in relative position RMSE and 30% reduction in attitude error compared to baseline dual quaternion filter\n\n### 2. **Deep Quaternion Networks**\n- **Authors:** Chase J. Gaudet & Anthony S. Maida (2018)\n- **Published in:** arXiv\n- **Key Contribution:** Extends deep learning to hyper-complex numbers (quaternions) with full quaternion operations in neural networks.\n- **Architecture Components:**\n  - Quaternion convolution layers\n  - Quaternion batch normalization (using Cholesky decomposition for 4D whitening)\n  - Quaternion weight initialization schemes\n  - Demonstrates improved convergence with fewer parameters compared to real and complex-valued networks\n- **Applications:** Tested on CIFAR-10/100 classification and KITTI road segmentation\n\n### 3. **Quaternion Graph Neural Networks (QGNN)**\n- **Authors:** Dai Quoc Nguyen et al. (2021)\n- **Published in:** ACML 2021\n- **Key Contribution:** Extends graph neural networks to quaternion space for knowledge graph embeddings.\n- **Architecture:** Implements dual quaternion graph neural networks with encoder-decoder style message passing in quaternion space\n- **Applications:** Knowledge graph completion, node classification, graph classification\n\n### 4. **Autoencoder-based Dimensionality Reduction for Accelerating PDE Solutions**\n- **Authors:** Diba Behnoudfar (2025)\n- **Published in:** arXiv\n- **Key Contribution:** Uses convolutional autoencoders for nonlinear dimensionality reduction of parametric PDE systems.\n- **Architecture:**\n  - Encoder: Contracting blocks with convolutions and max pooling\n  - Bottleneck: Linear layers mapping to reduced subspace (dimensions 4, 6, 8)\n  - Decoder: Expanding blocks with transposed convolutions\n- **Results:** Achieves MSE of order 1e-3 for validation data on porous media combustion problems\n\n## General Autoencoder Dimensionality Reduction\n\nWhile not specifically using dual quaternions, these papers provide foundational context:\n\n- **Hinton & Salakhutdinov (2006):** Demonstrated deep autoencoders outperform PCA for nonlinear dimensionality reduction\n- **Wang et al. (2016):** Comprehensive analysis of autoencoder dimensionality reduction capabilities compared to PCA, LDA, LLE, and Isomap\n- **Fournier et al. (2019):** Empirical comparison showing PCA remains competitive with autoencoders for classification tasks despite autoencoders' flexibility\n\n## Key Insights\n\nThe intersection of dual quaternions and machine learning is an emerging field with applications primarily in:\n- **Robotics and aerospace** (pose estimation, spacecraft navigation)\n- **Computer vision** (3D rotations, color image processing)\n- **Graph representation learning** (knowledge graphs)\n- **Scientific computing** (reduced-order modeling of PDEs)\n\nThe encoder-decoder architecture naturally fits dual quaternion representations because:\n1. Dual quaternions compactly encode 6-DOF motion (8 parameters with constraints)\n2. Encoder-decoder structures can learn to compress and reconstruct these representations\n3. Physics-informed losses can enforce dual quaternion algebraic constraints during training\n\n**Sources:**\n- Soh, W., & Lee, R. (2026). Neural Net Based Dual Quaternion Stochastic Filtering for Relative Spacecraft Motion Estimation. Journal of the Astronautical Sciences, 73, 44. https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s40295-026-00581-3\n- Gaudet, C. J., & Maida, A. S. (2018). Deep Quaternion Networks. arXiv:1712.04604. https://arxiv.org/pdf/1712.04604\n- Nguyen, D. Q., et al. (2021). Quaternion Graph Neural Networks. Asian Conference on Machine Learning. https://github.com/daiquocnguyen/QGNN\n- Behnoudfar, D. (2025). Autoencoder-based Dimensionality Reduction for Accelerating the Solution of Nonlinear Time-Dependent PDEs. arXiv:2505.09071. https://arxiv.org/html/2505.09071v1","type":"text"}],"id":"66a0094086c544ec8afda0edd45c61bc","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":68204,"input_tokens":19970,"output_tokens":1230}}
