2026-06-03T02:25:30.257796Z  INFO ThreadId(14) universal_search_service::service: 685: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, here is a comprehensive overview of **DualE (Dual Quaternion Knowledge Graph Embeddings)**:\n\n## DualE: Dual Quaternion Knowledge Graph Embeddings\n\n### Overview\nDualE is a knowledge graph embedding model introduced by Cao et al. (2021) at AAAI-21. It leverages **dual quaternion algebra** to represent entities and relations in a unified 8-dimensional hypercomplex space, enabling the modeling of both **rotation and translation** operations within a single framework.\n\n### Key Innovation\nThe core insight is that most existing knowledge graph embedding methods model relations as either pure translation (e.g., TransE) or pure rotation (e.g., RotatE, QuatE). DualE unifies both by representing relations as **compositions of translation and rotation** using dual quaternions.\n\n### Dual Quaternion Background\nA dual quaternion is defined as:\n```\nQ = a + εb\n```\nwhere `a` and `b` are quaternions (each with 4 components), and `ε` is a dual unit with `ε² = 0`. This gives an 8-dimensional representation:\n```\nQ = (a₀, a₁, a₂, a₃, b₀, b₁, b₂, b₃)\n```\n\nDual quaternions have a clear geometric interpretation: they can represent rigid body transformations (rotation + translation) in 3D space.\n\n### How DualE Works\n\n1. **Entity Embeddings**: Each entity is represented as a dual quaternion vector in `H^k_d` (dual quaternion space of dimension k).\n\n2. **Relation Embeddings**: Each relation is also a dual quaternion, which is normalized to a unit dual quaternion `W*_r` to avoid scaling effects.\n\n3. **Transformation**: For a triple `(h, r, t)`, the head entity embedding `Q_h` is transformed by the relation through dual quaternion multiplication:\n   ```\n   Q'_h = Q_h ⊗ W*_r\n   ```\n   This operation simultaneously applies rotation (from the real quaternion part) and translation (from the dual quaternion part).\n\n4. **Scoring Function**: The plausibility of a triple is computed using the dual quaternion inner product:\n   ```\n   φ(h,r,t) = ⟨Q'_h, Q_t⟩\n   ```\n   which expands to the sum of inner products of corresponding components.\n\n5. **Loss Function**: Cross-entropy loss with L2 regularization, optimized using negative sampling (Adagrad optimizer).\n\n### Theoretical Properties\n\nDualE satisfies all key relation patterns:\n- **Symmetry/Antisymmetry**\n- **Inversion**\n- **Composition**\n- **Multiple Relations** (different relations between same entity pair)\n\nIt is proven to be a **unified framework** that can degenerate into both rotation-family models (like RotatE) and translation-family models (like TransE), but neither family can derive DualE.\n\n### Advantages\n\n1. **Unified Framework**: First model to combine translation and rotation in a single, elegant mathematical formulation.\n2. **Rich Representation**: 8D dual quaternion space provides more expressive power than 4D quaternions (QuatE) or 2D complex numbers (RotatE).\n3. **Geometric Interpretation**: Clear physical meaning as rigid transformations in 3D space.\n4. **Pattern Coverage**: Can model all fundamental relation patterns plus multiple relations.\n\n### Experimental Results\n\nEvaluated on four benchmark datasets (WN18, FB15K, WN18RR, FB15K-237), DualE consistently outperformed state-of-the-art models including RotatE, QuatE, ComplEx-N3, TuckER, and ROTH. Notably, DualE achieved superior performance even with fewer dimensions than some baselines, demonstrating its efficiency.\n\n### Implementation\n\nThe official code is available at: https://github.com/Lion-ZS/DualE\n\nDualE is also integrated into the DICE Embeddings framework, which provides a unified interface for training and evaluating various knowledge graph embedding models.\n\n### References\n\n- Cao, Z., Xu, Q., Yang, Z., Cao, X., & Huang, Q. (2021). Dual Quaternion Knowledge Graph Embeddings. *Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence*, 35(8), 6894–6902. https://doi.org/10.1609/aaai.v35i8.16850\n- DICE Embeddings Documentation: https://deepwiki.com/dice-group/dice-embeddings/6.8-dual-quaternion-models\n\nThis research represents a significant advance in knowledge graph representation learning by bridging the gap between translation-based and rotation-based approaches through the elegant mathematics of dual quaternions.","type":"text"}],"id":"7dc7297dbdfc4a8385918027286d85f8","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":32516,"input_tokens":12040,"output_tokens":1036}}
