2026-06-05T10:41:57.366239Z  INFO ThreadId(11) universal_search_service::service: 685: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, here's a comprehensive explanation of the `--jinja` and `--special` flags in llama.cpp and their differences regarding chat template and special token handling:\n\n## `--jinja` Flag\n\n**Purpose:** Controls whether to use the Jinja2 template engine for chat formatting.\n\n**Default:** Enabled by default in most tools (llama-cli, llama-server)\n\n**Functionality:**\n- When enabled, uses the Jinja2 template engine (minja) to process chat templates stored in the model's metadata (`tokenizer.chat_template`)\n- Allows for complex template logic including loops, conditionals, and filters\n- Supports custom templates via `--chat-template` or `--chat-template-file`\n- Required for advanced features like tool calling, reasoning extraction, and complex message formatting\n\n**When to use:**\n- When working with models that have Jinja2 chat templates in their metadata\n- When you need to use custom chat templates\n- When you want to enable advanced features like reasoning/thinking extraction or tool calling\n\n## `--special` Flag\n\n**Purpose:** Controls whether special tokens are included in the output.\n\n**Default:** Disabled by default\n\n**Functionality:**\n- When enabled, outputs special tokens like `","type":"text"}],"id":"96e55c80624244ac96f63fa71de25ed9","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"<|im_start|>","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":74932,"input_tokens":10821,"output_tokens":260}}
