2026-06-05T10:42:57.557385Z  INFO ThreadId(17) universal_search_service::service: 685: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, I can provide a comprehensive overview of `llama.cpp`'s `--reasoning-format` feature, particularly for DeepSeek and Nemotron models, as of 2025-2026.\n\n## `--reasoning-format` in llama.cpp\n\nThe `--reasoning-format` flag controls how reasoning/thinking tags (like `<think>`) are parsed and returned in API responses. It was introduced to handle the \"chain of thought\" reasoning capabilities of models like DeepSeek-R1 and NVIDIA's Nemotron series.\n\n### Available Options\n\nAccording to the official llama.cpp server documentation, the flag accepts these values:\n\n- **`none`** – Leaves thoughts unparsed in `message.content` (default behavior before the feature)\n- **`deepseek`** – Extracts thoughts and puts them in `message.reasoning_content` (clean separation)\n- **`deepseek-legacy`** – Keeps `<think>` tags in `message.content` while also populating `message.reasoning_content`\n- **`auto`** (default) – Automatically detects from the model's chat template\n\n### Usage Example\n\n```bash\nllama-server -m model.gguf --reasoning-format deepseek\n```\n\n### How It Works\n\nWhen `--reasoning-format deepseek` is set:\n\n1. The server parses the model's output for `<think>` and `</think>` tags\n2. Content between these tags is extracted into a separate `reasoning_content` field in the API response\n3. The final answer appears in the standard `content` field\n\nThis matches the DeepSeek API's format and is now supported for Nemotron models as well.\n\n### Nemotron Support\n\nNVIDIA's Nemotron-3-Nano-30B-A3B and other Nemotron models support reasoning via the same `<think>` tag mechanism. To enable proper parsing:\n\n```bash\nllama-server -m Nemotron-3-Nano-30B-A3B.gguf \\\n  --jinja \\\n  --chat-template-kwargs '{\"enable_thinking\":true}' \\\n  --reasoning-format deepseek\n```\n\nUsers have confirmed that upgrading to recent versions of llama.cpp (build 7442+) properly places thinking content into the `reasoning_content` field for Nemotron models.\n\n### Related Flags\n\n- **`--reasoning [on|off|auto]`** – Controls whether reasoning/thinking is used (default: auto)\n- **`--reasoning-budget N`** – Sets a token budget for thinking (-1 = unrestricted, 0 = immediate end)\n- **`--chat-template-kwargs`** – Pass additional parameters like `{\"enable_thinking\":true}` to the template engine\n\n### Implementation Details\n\nThe feature is implemented in the chat template parsing system (`common/chat.cpp`, `common/chat-auto-parser-generator.cpp`). It uses an \"autoparser\" that analyzes the Jinja template to create a PEG parser capable of extracting reasoning content from model outputs.\n\n### Sources\n\n- [llama.cpp server README](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/tree/master/tools/server) – Official documentation for `--reasoning-format`\n- [Nemotron-3-Nano discussion on Hugging Face](https://huggingface.co/unsloth/Nemotron-3-Nano-30B-A3B-GGUF/discussions/3) – User reports on reasoning_content support\n- [Llama-Nemotron technical report](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2505.00949v3) – Details on reasoning toggle and `<think>` tag usage\n- [Chat Templates and Message Parsing DeepWiki](https://deepwiki.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/3.9-chat-templates-and-message-parsing) – Technical overview of the reasoning parsing system","type":"text"}],"id":"d6aa1e92e6cf478fbc7e08097c3f5740","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":84088,"input_tokens":34194,"output_tokens":814}}
