2026-06-05T13:41:08.976947Z  INFO ThreadId(10) universal_search_service::service: 685: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, I can provide you with a comprehensive guide on converting and using multimodal projectors (mmproj) with llama.cpp, including specific information about Nemotron Omni models.\n\n## **Converting Multimodal Projectors to GGUF for llama.cpp**\n\n### **1. Basic Concept**\n\nMultimodal inference in llama.cpp requires **two separate GGUF files**:\n- **Text model GGUF** (`model.gguf`) - The language model backbone\n- **Multimodal projector GGUF** (`mmproj.gguf`) - Contains vision/audio encoders and projection layers\n\nThe projector bridges the gap between media encoders (Vision Transformers, Audio Encoders) and the text model's embedding space.\n\n### **2. Conversion Process**\n\n#### **Using `convert_hf_to_gguf.py`**\n\nThe standard conversion script from llama.cpp supports multimodal projectors:\n\n```bash\n# Convert the text model\npython convert_hf_to_gguf.py /path/to/model \\\n  --outtype f16 \\\n  --outfile model-f16.gguf\n\n# Convert the multimodal projector (note the --mmproj flag)\npython convert_hf_to_gguf.py /path/to/model \\\n  --mmproj \\\n  --outtype f16 \\\n  --outfile mmproj-f16.gguf\n```\n\n**Key Points:**\n- The `--mmproj` flag tells the converter to extract only the multimodal projector components\n- Projectors are typically kept at higher precision (F16/BF16) to preserve cross-modal alignment quality\n- The text model can be quantized independently (Q4_K_M, Q5_K_M, etc.)\n\n#### **Quantization**\n\nAfter conversion, you can quantize the text model:\n\n```bash\n# Quantize text model to Q4_K_M\n./llama-quantize model-f16.gguf model-Q4_K_M.gguf Q4_K_M\n\n# Keep mmproj at F16 (recommended)\n# No quantization needed for mmproj\n```\n\n### **3. Usage with llama.cpp**\n\n#### **Command Line**\n```bash\nllama-mtmd-cli \\\n  -m model-Q4_K_M.gguf \\\n  --mmproj mmproj-f16.gguf \\\n  --image input.jpg \\\n  -p \"Describe this image\"\n```\n\n#### **Server Mode**\n```bash\nllama-server \\\n  --model model-Q4_K_M.gguf \\\n  --mmproj mmproj-f16.gguf \\\n  --host 0.0.0.0 \\\n  --port 8080\n```\n\n### **4. Nemotron Omni Specifics**\n\nFor **Nemotron-3-Nano-Omni-30B-A3B** (vision + audio + video):\n\n#### **Available GGUF Variants**\nThe model has been converted by the community with multiple quantization options:\n- **Text model**: Various quantizations (Q2_K to Q8_0, IQ4_XS, MXFP4_MOE)\n- **mmproj**: Typically F16 or BF16 to preserve encoder quality\n\nExample from Hugging Face:\n- Text: `NVIDIA-Nemotron-3-Nano-Omni-30B-A3B-Reasoning-UD-Q4_K_XL.gguf`\n- mmproj: `mmproj-BF16.gguf`\n\n#### **Important Notes for Nemotron Omni**\n1. **CUDA Compatibility**: Avoid CUDA 13.2 (produces gibberish). Use CUDA 12.x or Metal/CPU\n2. **Memory Requirements**: \n   - 4-bit quantized: ~25GB RAM\n   - 8-bit quantized: ~36GB RAM\n3. **Modality Support**:\n   - **Vision**: CRADIO v4-H encoder\n   - **Audio**: Parakeet-TDT-0.6B-v2 encoder  \n   - **Video**: Parakeet + frame sampler (≤2 min, 256 frames @ 2 FPS)\n\n### **5. Architecture Support**\n\nllama.cpp's `libmtmd` supports various multimodal architectures:\n\n| Model Family | Vision | Audio | Mixed |\n|-------------|--------|-------|-------|\n| LLaVA 1.5/1.6 | ✓ | | |\n| Qwen2-VL/Qwen3-VL | ✓ | | |\n| Gemma 3/4 | ✓ | | ✓ |\n| InternVL | ✓ | | |\n| Ultravox | | ✓ | |\n| **Nemotron Omni** | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |\n\n### **6. Common Issues & Solutions**\n\n**Issue**: \"mmproj not found\"\n- **Solution**: Ensure you're using the correct mmproj file that matches your text model family\n\n**Issue**: Poor multimodal performance\n- **Solution**: Keep mmproj at F16/BF16 precision; avoid quantizing the projector\n\n**Issue**: Out of memory\n- **Solution**: Use `--no-mmproj-offload` to keep projector on CPU, or reduce context size\n\n**Issue**: CUDA errors with Nemotron\n- **Solution**: Pin to CUDA 12.x or use CPU/Metal backend\n\n### **7. Best Practices**\n\n1. **Always pair matching models**: The mmproj must be trained for the specific text model architecture\n2. **Preserve projector precision**: Keep mmproj at F16/BF16 for best quality\n3. **Test with small images first**: Before processing large batches\n4. **Monitor memory**: Multimodal processing increases memory usage significantly\n5. **Use appropriate context**: Some models require large context windows (e.g., 8192+)\n\n### **Sources & References**\n\n- [llama.cpp Multimodal Documentation](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/blob/master/docs/multimodal.md)\n- [Nemotron-3-Nano-Omni GGUF on Hugging Face](https://huggingface.co/majentik/Nemotron-3-Nano-Omni-30B-A3B-Reasoning-mmproj-F16)\n- [Unsloth Nemotron 3 Nano Omni Guide](https://unsloth.ai/docs/models/nemotron-3-nano-omni)\n- [Model Conversion from HuggingFace](https://deepwiki.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/7.2-model-conversion-from-huggingface)\n\nThis comprehensive approach should help you successfully convert and use multimodal projectors with llama.cpp, including the advanced Nemotron Omni models with vision, audio, and video capabilities.","type":"text"}],"id":"840d055f0173474ab6f4d02d5adb7994","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":58108,"input_tokens":38957,"output_tokens":1439}}
