2026-06-08T11:51:57.286835Z  INFO ThreadId(17) universal_search_service::service: 685: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, I can provide you with comprehensive guidance on how to prompt NVIDIA's Nemotron and Parakeet Conformer ASR models for speech recognition.\n\n## Key Models\n\nNVIDIA offers several state-of-the-art ASR models:\n\n1. **Nemotron Speech Streaming** (600M parameters) - Optimized for real-time streaming with cache-aware FastConformer-RNNT architecture\n2. **Parakeet Family** - Includes CTC, RNNT, and TDT variants in 0.6B and 1.1B sizes\n3. **Canary** - Multitask model supporting ASR and translation\n\n## Basic Usage (No Prompting Required)\n\nThese models are **not prompted like LLMs**. They are specialized speech-to-text models that transcribe audio directly. Here's the simplest approach:\n\n```python\nimport nemo.collections.asr as nemo_asr\n\n# Load model\nasr_model = nemo_asr.models.ASRModel.from_pretrained(\n    model_name=\"nvidia/nemotron-speech-streaming-en-0.6b\"\n)\n\n# Transcribe audio\ntranscript = asr_model.transcribe([\"path/to/audio.wav\"])[0].text\nprint(transcript)\n```\n\n## Advanced Configuration\n\n### 1. **Timestamp Generation**\n```python\n# Get word-level timestamps\nhypotheses = asr_model.transcribe([\"audio.wav\"], timestamps=True)\nword_timestamps = hypotheses[0].timestamp['word']\nfor stamp in word_timestamps:\n    print(f\"{stamp['start']:.2f}s - {stamp['end']:.2f}s: {stamp['word']}\")\n```\n\n### 2. **Streaming Configuration (Nemotron)**\nFor low-latency streaming, configure chunk size via `att_context_size` (measured in 80ms frames):\n\n```python\n# Chunk sizes: [70,0]=80ms, [70,1]=160ms, [70,6]=560ms, [70,13]=1120ms\n# Lower latency = smaller chunks but potentially higher WER\n```\n\n### 3. **Decoding Strategy**\n```python\nfrom omegaconf import OmegaConf, open_dict\n\n# Modify decoding config\ndecoding_cfg = asr_model.cfg.decoding\nwith open_dict(decoding_cfg):\n    decoding_cfg.strategy = \"beam\"  # or \"greedy\"\n    decoding_cfg.beam.beam_size = 10\n    asr_model.change_decoding_strategy(decoding_cfg)\n```\n\n### 4. **Batch Inference**\n```python\n# Transcribe multiple files\naudio_files = [\"file1.wav\", \"file2.wav\", \"file3.wav\"]\ntranscripts = asr_model.transcribe(audio_files, batch_size=32)\n```\n\n## Command Line Usage\n\n```bash\npython examples/asr/transcribe_speech.py \\\n    pretrained_name=\"nvidia/nemotron-speech-streaming-en-0.6b\" \\\n    audio_dir=\"/path/to/audio/directory\" \\\n    batch_size=32 \\\n    compute_timestamps=True\n```\n\n## API Access (No Local Setup)\n\nUse NVIDIA's hosted API via Riva client:\n\n```python\nimport riva.client\n\nauth = riva.client.Auth(\n    uri=\"grpc.nvcf.nvidia.com:443\",\n    use_ssl=True,\n    metadata_args=[\n        [\"function-id\", \"bb0837de-8c7b-481f-9ec8-ef5663e9c1fa\"],\n        [\"authorization\", \"Bearer nvapi-YOUR_API_KEY\"],\n    ],\n)\n\nasr_service = riva.client.ASRService(auth)\nwith open(\"audio.wav\", \"rb\") as f:\n    audio = f.read()\n\nconfig = riva.client.RecognitionConfig(\n    language_code=\"en-US\",\n    enable_automatic_punctuation=True,\n    enable_word_time_offsets=True,\n)\n\nresponse = asr_service.offline_recognize(audio, config)\nprint(response.results[0].alternatives[0].transcript)\n```\n\n## Performance Considerations\n\n- **Chunk size trade-off**: Smaller chunks (80ms) give lower latency but slightly higher WER; larger chunks (1.12s) improve accuracy\n- **Batch size**: Increase for throughput, decrease for memory constraints\n- **Model selection**: \n  - Use **Nemotron Streaming** for real-time applications\n  - Use **Parakeet CTC** for large-scale batch processing (fastest RTF)\n  - Use **Parakeet RNNT** for highest accuracy\n\n## Important Notes\n\n1. These models are **English-only** (as of current versions)\n2. They automatically handle punctuation and capitalization\n3. No text prompts are needed - the model directly converts audio to text\n4. For custom domains/accents, fine-tuning is recommended\n\n## Sources\n\n- [NVIDIA NeMo ASR Documentation](https://docs.nvidia.com/nemo-framework/user-guide/latest/nemotoolkit/asr/intro.html)\n- [Nemotron Speech Streaming Model Card](https://huggingface.co/nvidia/nemotron-speech-streaming-en-0.6b)\n- [NeMo GitHub Repository](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/NeMo)","type":"text"}],"id":"faa0d566f0f64a97ba4fc84a2737e05c","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":51188,"input_tokens":8092,"output_tokens":1166}}
