2026-06-08T11:52:27.339659Z  INFO ThreadId(16) universal_search_service::service: 685: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, **yes, Nemotron Omni (specifically Nemotron 3 Nano Omni) does support ASR (Automatic Speech Recognition) speech-to-text capabilities as a core part of its multimodal functionality.**\n\nHere are the key details:\n\n## Audio/ASR Capabilities\n\nNemotron 3 Nano Omni is designed as a **unified multimodal model** that natively processes text, images, video, and **audio** in a single system. It includes strong speech understanding capabilities that enable high-quality transcription across diverse audio conditions.\n\n### Key Features:\n- **Native audio input processing** (not just text transcripts)\n- Handles long-form audio with varying speakers, accents, and background noise\n- Supports audio inputs up to **1,200 seconds (20 minutes)** during training, with context length supporting 5+ hours\n- Audio is sampled at 16 kHz and processed through the **Parakeet-TDT-0.6B-v2** audio encoder\n\n### Performance on ASR Benchmarks:\nThe model achieves competitive results on standard ASR benchmarks:\n- **OpenASR average WER**: 5.95 (lower is better)\n- Outperforms comparable models like Qwen3-Omni (6.55 WER) on the OpenASR benchmark\n- Strong performance across multiple datasets including AMI, Earnings22, GigaSpeech, LibriSpeech, SPGISpeech, TED-LIUM, and VoxPopuli\n\n### Integration with Other Modalities:\nThe ASR capabilities are designed to work seamlessly with other modalities:\n- Transcribed spoken content can be analyzed and combined with visual information\n- Enables tasks like summarization, question answering, and cross-modal reasoning\n- Particularly useful for scenarios like narrated screen recordings, video Q&A, meetings with slides, and long-form instructional content\n\n## Architecture\nThe model uses a hybrid Mamba-Transformer Mixture-of-Experts backbone (30B total, 3B active parameters) with separate encoders for each modality that feed into a unified language model decoder. This allows genuine cross-modal reasoning within the backbone itself.\n\n**Sources:**\n- NVIDIA Blog: \"NVIDIA Launches Nemotron 3 Nano Omni Model, Unifying Vision, Audio and...\" (https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/nemotron-3-nano-omni-multimodal-ai-agents/)\n- Hugging Face Blog: \"Introducing NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Nano Omni: Long-Context Multimodal Intelligence for Documents, Audio and Video Agents\" (https://huggingface.co/blog/nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-omni-multimodal-intelligence)\n- arXiv Technical Report: \"Nemotron 3 Nano Omni: Efficient and Open Multimodal Intelligence\" (https://arxiv.org/html/2604.24954v1)\n- GitHub Repository: NVIDIA-NeMo/Nemotron (https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Nemotron)","type":"text"}],"id":"eda66feb6c044b68aae8ef91c91ffb03","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":54364,"output_tokens":633}}
