2026-06-08T11:53:17.479867Z  INFO ThreadId(11) universal_search_service::service: 685: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on the official NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Nano Omni documentation, here's how to prompt speech transcription with audio input:\n\n## Audio Input Format\n\nThe model accepts audio files in **WAV or MP3 format** (up to 1 hour duration) with sampling rates of **8kHz or higher**.\n\n## Chat Template Structure\n\nFor audio input, you need to use the multimodal content format with `audio_url`:\n\n```python\n{\n    \"role\": \"user\",\n    \"content\": [\n        {\"type\": \"audio_url\", \"audio_url\": {\"url\": \"file_path_or_url\"}},\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Transcription instruction\"}\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n## Complete Example (Python with OpenAI client)\n\n```python\nfrom openai import OpenAI\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nclient = OpenAI(base_url=\"http://localhost:8000/v1\", api_key=\"\")\nMODEL = \"nvidia/Nemotron-3-Nano-Omni-30B-A3B-Reasoning-NVFP4\"\n\n# Convert local file to file:// URL\naudio_url = Path(\"media/2414-165385-0000.wav\").resolve().as_uri()\n\nresponse = client.chat.completions.create(\n    model=MODEL,\n    messages=[\n        {\n            \"role\": \"user\",\n            \"content\": [\n                {\"type\": \"audio_url\", \"audio_url\": {\"url\": audio_url}},\n                {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Transcribe this audio.\"},\n            ],\n        }\n    ],\n    max_tokens=1024,\n    temperature=1.0,\n    extra_body={\"top_k\": 1, \"chat_template_kwargs\": {\"enable_thinking\": False}},\n)\nprint(response.choices[0].message.content)\n```\n\n## Key Parameters for ASR Tasks\n\n- **For transcription**: Use **non-thinking mode** (`enable_thinking: False`)\n- **Recommended sampling**: `temperature=0.2`, `top_k=1`\n- **Output**: The model supports **word-level timestamps** for transcription\n\n## Server Setup (vLLM)\n\nIf you're running the model locally with vLLM, ensure you install audio support:\n\n```bash\npython3 -m pip install \"vllm[audio]\"\n```\n\nThen serve with appropriate flags:\n\n```bash\nvllm serve nvidia/Nemotron-3-Nano-Omni-30B-A3B-Reasoning-NVFP4 \\\n  --host 0.0.0.0 \\\n  --max-model-len 131072 \\\n  --trust-remote-code \\\n  --allowed-local-media-path /\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n1. Audio URLs can be local file paths converted to `file://` URLs (using `Path.resolve().as_uri()`)\n2. The model supports various audio tasks beyond transcription, including audio understanding and Q&A\n3. For best transcription results, use the recommended non-thinking mode parameters\n\n**Source**: [NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Nano Omni Model Card](https://build.nvidia.com/nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-omni-30b-a3b-reasoning/modelcard)","type":"text"}],"id":"9f8244b8b34b490ead9358ad47317393","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":45844,"input_tokens":16647,"output_tokens":715}}
