2026-06-08T16:32:43.078196Z  INFO ThreadId(16) universal_search_service::service: 685: Claude API response: {"content":[{"thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Based on my research, here is the information about the multimodal chat template placeholder in llama.cpp's `libmtmd`:\n\n## Multimodal Chat Template Placeholder\n\nIn llama.cpp's multimodal system (`libmtmd`), the placeholder used to mark where images or audio should be inserted in the text prompt is:\n\n**`<__media__>`** (default marker)\n\n### Key Details:\n\n1. **Default Marker**: The default media marker is defined by `mtmd_default_marker()` and is `\"<__media__>\"`.\n\n2. **Usage**: When tokenizing a mixed text+media prompt, you must include this marker in the text where you want the image/audio to appear. For example:\n   ```\n   \"Describe this image: <__media__>\\nBe specific.\"\n   ```\n\n3. **Tokenization Process**: The `mtmd_tokenize()` function (from `tools/mtmd/mtmd.h`) splits the prompt into ordered text and media chunks:\n   - It requires that the number of bitmaps (images/audio) matches the number of markers in the prompt\n   - The marker gets replaced with the actual encoded media embeddings during processing\n\n4. **Customization**: The marker can be customized via the `mtmd_context_params` structure when initializing the multimodal context:\n   ```c\n   struct mtmd_context_params {\n       const char * media_marker; // customizable marker\n       // ... other parameters\n   };\n   ```\n\n5. **Implementation**: This is handled in the `mtmd_tokenize()` function which parses the input text, finds all occurrences of the marker, and creates corresponding chunks that interleave text tokens with media embeddings.\n\n### Source References:\n- `tools/mtmd/mtmd.h` lines 158-228 (function signatures)\n- `tools/mtmd/mtmd.cpp` lines 802-809 (tokenize implementation)\n- The comment in `mtmd.h` explains: *\"the prompt must have the input image marker (default: `<__media__>`) in it\"*\n\nThis placeholder system allows `libmtmd` to maintain a clean separation between text and media processing while supporting various model architectures with different chat template requirements.","type":"text"}],"id":"d65852e6a174438d9cfec4fa8e8aac00","model":"kat-coder-pro-v2","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"stop_sequence","stop_sequence":"248046","type":"message","usage":{"cache_read_input_tokens":69748,"input_tokens":8221,"output_tokens":471}}
